    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">Duplicate: avatar (2 variants) -> ns</p>
    "! - sap.m.Avatar (ns='')
    "! - Aggregation <avatar> (ns='')
    "! Namespace prefixes: '' = sap.m, 'core' = sap.ui.core, 'mvc' = sap.ui.core.mvc, 'l' = sap.ui.layout, 'form' = sap.ui.layout.form, 'table' = sap.ui.table
    "! @parameter ns                           | (string) Namespace prefix. Allowed '', 'core', 'mvc', 'l', 'form', 'table'
    "!                         ('' is sap.m default). Variants: sap.m.Avatar ('') | aggregation:avatar
    "!                         (''). Pass prefix directly.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter src                          | (sap.ui.core.URI) Determines the path to the desired image or icon.
    "! @parameter initials                     | (string) Defines the displayed initials. They should consist of only 1,2 or
    "!                         3 latin letters.
    "! @parameter display_shape                | (sap.m.AvatarShape) Defines the shape of the Avatar . Default: Circle.
    "! @parameter display_size                 | (sap.m.AvatarSize) Sets a predefined display size of the Avatar . Default:
    "!                         S.
    "! @parameter custom_display_size          | (sap.ui.core.CSSSize) Specifies custom display size of the Avatar . Note:
    "!                         It takes effect if the displaySize property is set to Custom . Default:
    "!                         3rem.
    "! @parameter custom_font_size             | (sap.ui.core.CSSSize) Specifies custom font size of the Avatar . Note: It
    "!                         takes effect if the displaySize property is set to Custom . Default:
    "!                         1.125rem.
    "! @parameter image_fit_type               | (sap.m.AvatarImageFitType) Specifies how an image would fit in the Avatar .
    "!                         Default: Cover.
    "! @parameter fallback_icon                | (string) Defines the fallback icon displayed in case of wrong image src and
    "!                         no initials set. Notes: If not set, a default fallback icon is displayed
    "!                         depending on the set displayShape property. Accepted values are only icons
    "!                         from the SAP icon font.
    "! @parameter background_color             | (sap.m.AvatarColor) Determines the background color of the control.
    "!                         Default: Accent6.
    "! @parameter show_border                  | (boolean) Determines whether the control is displayed with border. Default:
    "!                         false.
    "! @parameter badge_icon                   | (sap.ui.core.URI) Defines what type of icon is displayed as visual
    "!                         affordance. It can be predefined or custom. The predefined icons are
    "!                         recommended for: Suggesting a zooming action: sap-icon://zoom-in Suggesting
    "!                         an image change: sap-icon://camera Suggesting an editing action:
    "!                         sap-icon://edit Notes: Use sap-icon://avatar-icon-none to show the badge
    "!                         without an icon. When using avatar-icon-none, the badge remains visible and
    "!                         can display background color or tooltip.
    "! @parameter badge_tooltip                | (string) Defines a custom tooltip for the badgeIcon . If set, it overrides
    "!                         the available default values. If not set, default tooltips are used as
    "!                         follows: Specific default tooltips are displayed for each of the predefined
    "!                         badgeIcons . For any other icons, the displayed tooltip is the same as the
    "!                         main control tooltip.
    "! @parameter decorative                   | (boolean) Defines whether the sap.m.Avatar is used for decorative purposes
    "!                         and is ignored by accessibility tools. Note: This property doesn't take
    "!                         effect if sap.m.Avatar has a press handler. Default: false.
    "! @parameter aria_has_popup               | (sap.ui.core.aria.HasPopup) Specifies the value of the aria-haspopup
    "!                         attribute If the value is None , the attribute will not be rendered.
    "!                         Otherwise it will be rendered with the selected value. NOTE: Use this
    "!                         property only when an avatar is related to a popover/popup. The value needs
    "!                         to be equal to the main/root role of the popup - e.g. dialog, menu or list
    "!                         (examples: if you have dialog -> dialog, if you have menu -> menu; if you
    "!                         have list -> list; if you have dialog containing a list -> dialog). Do not
    "!                         use it, if you open a standard sap.m.Dialog, MessageBox or other type of
    "!                         dialogs displayed as on overlay over the application. Default: None.
    "! @parameter badge_value_state            | (sap.ui.core.ValueState) Visualizes the validation state of the badge, e.g.
    "!                         Error , Warning , Success , Information . Default: None.
    "! @parameter badge_icon_color             | (sap.m.AvatarBadgeColor) Defines the color of the badge icon. This color is
    "!                         used to style the badge, indicating different statuses or categories.
    "!                         Acceptable values include predefined `sap.m.AvatarBadgeColor` options.
    "!                         Default: Accent6.
    "! @parameter enabled                      | (boolean) Determines whether the Avatar is enabled (default is set to true
    "!                         ). A disabled Button has different colors depending on the AvatarColor.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter active                       | (boolean) Determines whether the Avatar is active/toggled (default is set
    "!                         to false ). Active state is meant to be toggled when user clicks on the
    "!                         Avatar . The Active state is only applied, when the Avatar has press
    "!                         listeners. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) Fired when the user selects the control.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS avatar
      IMPORTING
        ns                           TYPE string OPTIONAL
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        src                          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        initials                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        display_shape                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        display_size                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        custom_display_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        custom_font_size             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        image_fit_type               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        fallback_icon                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        background_color             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_border                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        badge_icon                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        badge_tooltip                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        decorative                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        aria_has_popup               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        badge_value_state            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        badge_icon_color             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enabled                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        active                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        press                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

