    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.FeedInput</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.FeedInput
    "! The Feed Input allows the user to enter text for a new feed entry and then post
    "! it.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter enabled                      | (boolean) Set this flag to "false" to disable both text input and post
    "!                         button. Default: true.
    "! @parameter rows                         | (int) Defines the number of visible text lines for the control. Note:
    "!                         Minimum value is 2, maximum value is 15. Default: 2.
    "! @parameter show_exceeded_text           | (boolean) Determines whether the characters, exceeding the maximum allowed
    "!                         character count, are visible in the input field. If set to false , the user
    "!                         is not allowed to enter more characters than what is set in the maxLength
    "!                         property. If set to true , the characters exceeding the maxLength value are
    "!                         selected on paste and the counter below the input field displays their
    "!                         number. Default: false.
    "! @parameter max_length                   | (int) The maximum length (the maximum number of characters) for the feed's
    "!                         input value. By default this is not limited. Default: 0.
    "! @parameter growing                      | (boolean) Indicates the ability of the control to automatically grow and
    "!                         shrink dynamically with its content. Default: false.
    "! @parameter growing_max_lines            | (int) Defines the maximum number of lines that the control can grow. Value
    "!                         is set to 0 by default, which means an unlimited numbers of rows. Note:
    "!                         Minimum value to set is equal to the rows property value, maximum value is
    "!                         15. Default: 0.
    "! @parameter placeholder                  | (string) The placeholder text shown in the input area as long as the user
    "!                         has not entered any text value. Default: Post something here.
    "! @parameter value                        | (string) The text value of the feed input. As long as the user has not
    "!                         entered any text the post button is disabled
    "! @parameter icon                         | (sap.ui.core.URI) Icon to be displayed as a graphical element within the
    "!                         feed input. This can be an image or an icon from the icon font.
    "! @parameter icon_display_shape           | (sap.m.AvatarShape) Defines the shape of the icon. Default: Circle.
    "! @parameter icon_initials                | (string) Defines the initials of the icon.
    "! @parameter icon_size                    | (sap.m.AvatarSize) Defines the size of the icon. Default: M.
    "! @parameter show_icon                    | (boolean) If set to "true" (default), icons will be displayed. In case no
    "!                         icon is provided the standard placeholder will be displayed. if set to
    "!                         "false" icons are hidden Default: true.
    "! @parameter button_tooltip               | (sap.ui.core.TooltipBase|string) Sets a new tooltip for Submit button. The
    "!                         tooltip can either be a simple string (which in most cases will be rendered
    "!                         as the title attribute of this element) or an instance of
    "!                         sap.ui.core.TooltipBase. If a new tooltip is set, any previously set
    "!                         tooltip is deactivated. The default value is set language dependent.
    "!                         Default: Submit.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter post                         | (event) The Post event is triggered when the user has entered a value and
    "!                         pressed the post button. After firing this event, the value is reset.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS feed_input
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enabled                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        rows                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_exceeded_text           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        max_length                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing_max_lines            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        placeholder                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        value                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon_display_shape           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon_initials                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon_size                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_icon                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        button_tooltip               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
