    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.NotificationList</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.NotificationList
    "! The NotificationList control provides a container for NotificationListGroup and
    "! NotificationListItem .
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter inset                        | (boolean) Defines the indentation of the container. Setting it to true
    "!                         indents the list. Default: false.
    "! @parameter header_text                  | (string) Defines the header text that appears in the control. Note: If the
    "!                         headerToolbar aggregation is set, then this property is ignored. If this is
    "!                         the case, use, for example, a sap.m.Title control in the toolbar to define
    "!                         a header.
    "! @parameter header_level                 | (sap.ui.core.TitleLevel) Defines the semantic header level of the header
    "!                         text (see headerText property ). This information is, for example, used by
    "!                         assistive technologies, such as screenreaders, to create a hierarchical
    "!                         site map for faster navigation. Depending on this setting, either the ARIA
    "!                         equivalent of an HTML h1-h6 element is used or, when using the Auto level,
    "!                         no explicit level information is used. Note: If the headerToolbar
    "!                         aggregation is set, then this property is ignored. If this is the case,
    "!                         use, for example, a sap.m.Title control in the toolbar to define a header.
    "!                         Default: Auto.
    "! @parameter footer_text                  | (string) Defines the footer text that appears in the control.
    "! @parameter mode                         | (sap.m.ListMode) Defines the mode of the control (e.g. None , SingleSelect
    "!                         , MultiSelect , Delete ). Default: None.
    "! @parameter width                        | (sap.ui.core.CSSSize) Sets the width of the control. Default: 100%.
    "! @parameter include_item_in_selection    | (boolean) Defines whether the items are selectable by clicking on the item
    "!                         itself ( true ) rather than having to set the selection control first.
    "!                         Note: The SingleSelectMaster mode also provides this functionality by
    "!                         default. Default: false.
    "! @parameter show_unread                  | (boolean) Activates the unread indicator for all items, if set to true .
    "!                         Default: false.
    "! @parameter no_data_text                 | (string) This text is displayed if the control contains no items. Note: If
    "!                         both a noDataText property and a noData aggregation are provided, the
    "!                         noData aggregation takes priority. If the noData aggregation is undefined
    "!                         or set to null, the noDataText property is used instead.
    "! @parameter show_no_data                 | (boolean) Defines whether or not the text specified in the noDataText
    "!                         property is displayed. Default: true.
    "! @parameter enable_busy_indicator        | (boolean) When this property is set to true , the control will
    "!                         automatically display a busy indicator when it detects that data is being
    "!                         loaded. This busy indicator blocks the interaction with the items until
    "!                         data loading is finished. By default, the busy indicator will be shown
    "!                         after one second. This behavior can be customized by setting the
    "!                         busyIndicatorDelay property. Default: true.
    "! @parameter mode_animation_on            | (boolean) Defines if animations will be shown while switching between
    "!                         modes. Default: true.
    "! @parameter show_separators              | (sap.m.ListSeparators) Defines which item separator style will be used.
    "!                         Default: All.
    "! @parameter swipe_direction              | (sap.m.SwipeDirection) Defines the direction of the swipe movement (e.g
    "!                         LeftToRight, RightToLeft, Both) to display the control defined in the
    "!                         swipeContent aggregation. Default: Both.
    "! @parameter growing                      | (boolean) If set to true , enables the growing feature of the control to
    "!                         load more items by requesting from the model. Note: : This feature only
    "!                         works when an items aggregation is bound. Growing must not be used together
    "!                         with two-way binding. Default: false.
    "! @parameter growing_threshold            | (int) Defines the number of items to be requested from the model for each
    "!                         grow. This property can only be used if the growing property is set to true
    "!                         . Default: 20.
    "! @parameter growing_trigger_text         | (string) Defines the text displayed on the growing button. The default is a
    "!                         translated text ("More") coming from the message bundle. This property can
    "!                         only be used if the growing property is set to true .
    "! @parameter growing_scroll_to_load       | (boolean) If set to true, the user can scroll down/up to load more items.
    "!                         Otherwise a growing button is displayed at the bottom/top of the control.
    "!                         Note: This property can only be used if the growing property is set to true
    "!                         and only if there is one instance of sap.m.List or sap.m.Table inside the
    "!                         scrollable scroll container (e.g sap.m.Page ). Default: false.
    "! @parameter growing_direction            | (sap.m.ListGrowingDirection) Defines the direction of the growing feature.
    "!                         If set to Downwards the user has to scroll down to load more items or the
    "!                         growing button is displayed at the bottom. If set to Upwards the user has
    "!                         to scroll up to load more items or the growing button is displayed at the
    "!                         top. Default: Downwards.
    "! @parameter remember_selections          | (boolean) If set to true, this control remembers and retains the selection
    "!                         of the items after a binding update has been performed (e.g. sorting,
    "!                         filtering). Note: This feature works only if two-way data binding for the
    "!                         selected property of the item is not used. It also needs to be turned off
    "!                         if the binding context of the item does not always point to the same entry
    "!                         in the model, for example, if the order of the data in the JSONModel is
    "!                         changed. Note: This feature leverages the built-in selection mechanism of
    "!                         the corresponding binding context if the OData V4 model is used. Therefore,
    "!                         all binding-relevant limitations apply in this context as well. For more
    "!                         details, see the setSelected, the bindList, and the requestValueListInfo
    "!                         API documentation. Do not enable this feature if $$sharedRequest or
    "!                         $$clearSelectionOnFilter is active. Note: If this property is set to false
    "!                         , a possible binding context update of items (for example, filtering or
    "!                         sorting the list binding) would clear the selection of the items. Default:
    "!                         true.
    "! @parameter keyboard_mode                | (sap.m.ListKeyboardMode) Defines keyboard handling behavior of the control.
    "!                         Default: Navigation.
    "! @parameter sticky                       | (sap.m.Sticky[]) Defines the section of the control that remains fixed at
    "!                         the top of the page during vertical scrolling as long as the control is in
    "!                         the viewport. Note: Enabling sticky column headers in List controls will
    "!                         not have any effect. There are some known restrictions. A few are given
    "!                         below: If the control is placed in layout containers that have the
    "!                         overflow: hidden or overflow: auto style definition, this can prevent the
    "!                         sticky elements of the control from becoming fixed at the top of the
    "!                         viewport. If sticky column headers are enabled in the sap.m.Table control,
    "!                         setting focus on the column headers will let the table scroll to the top. A
    "!                         transparent toolbar design is not supported for sticky bars. The toolbar
    "!                         will automatically get an intransparent background color. This feature
    "!                         supports only the default height of the toolbar control and the column
    "!                         headers. When sticky group headers are enabled, wrapping in the column
    "!                         headers is not supported.
    "! @parameter multi_select_mode            | (sap.m.MultiSelectMode) Defines the multi-selection mode for the control.
    "!                         If the property is set to ClearAll , then selecting items via the keyboard
    "!                         shortcut CTRL + A and via the selectAll method is not possible. See
    "!                         selectAll for more details. A selection of multiple items is still possible
    "!                         using the range selection feature. For more information about the range
    "!                         selection, see Keyboard Handling for Item Selection. Only relevant for
    "!                         sap.m.Table : If ClearAll is set, the table renders a Deselect All icon in
    "!                         the column header, otherwise a Select All checkbox is shown. The Select All
    "!                         checkbox allows the user to select all the items in the control, and the
    "!                         Deselect All icon deselects the items. Note: This property must be used
    "!                         with the MultiSelect mode. Default: Default.
    "! @parameter item_action_count            | (int) Defines the maximum number of actions displayed for the items. If the
    "!                         number of item actions exceeds the itemActionCount property value, an
    "!                         overflow button will appear, providing access to the additional actions.
    "!                         Note: Only values between 0-2 enables the use of the new actions
    "!                         aggregation. When enabled, the Delete mode and the Detail list item type
    "!                         have no effect. Instead, dedicated actions of type Delete or Edit should be
    "!                         used. Note: As of version 1.147, items with type Navigation render the
    "!                         navigation indicator as an action, which is not counted in itemActionCount
    "!                         . Default: -1.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter selection_change             | (event) Fires when selection is changed via user interaction inside the
    "!                         control.
    "! @parameter delete                       | (event) Fires when delete icon is pressed by user.
    "! @parameter swipe                        | (event) Fires after user's swipe action and before the swipeContent is
    "!                         shown. On the swipe event handler, swipeContent can be changed according to
    "!                         the swiped item. Calling the preventDefault method of the event cancels the
    "!                         swipe action. Note: There is no accessible alternative provided by the
    "!                         control for swiping. Applications that use this functionality must provide
    "!                         an accessible alternative UI to perform the same action.
    "! @parameter update_started               | (event) Fires before items binding is updated (e.g. sorting, filtering)
    "!                         Note: Event handler should not invalidate the control.
    "! @parameter update_finished              | (event) Fires after items binding is updated and processed by the control.
    "! @parameter item_press                   | (event) Fires when an item is pressed unless the item's type property is
    "!                         Inactive .
    "! @parameter before_open_context_menu     | (event) Fired when the context menu is opened. When the context menu is
    "!                         opened, the binding context of the item is set to the given contextMenu .
    "! @parameter item_action_press            | (event) Fired when an item action is pressed.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS notification_list
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        inset                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        header_text                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        header_level                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        footer_text                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        mode                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        width                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        include_item_in_selection    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_unread                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        no_data_text                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_no_data                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enable_busy_indicator        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        mode_animation_on            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_separators              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        swipe_direction              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing_threshold            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing_trigger_text         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing_scroll_to_load       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing_direction            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        remember_selections          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        keyboard_mode                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        sticky                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        multi_select_mode            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        item_action_count            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selection_change             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        delete                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        swipe                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        update_started               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        update_finished              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        item_press                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        before_open_context_menu     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        item_action_press            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        PREFERRED PARAMETER header_text
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.NotificationListGroup</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.NotificationListGroup
    "! The NotificationListGroup control is used for grouping notification items of the
    "! same type. Behavior The group handles specific behavior for different use cases:
    "! autoPriority - determines the group priority to the highest priority of an item
    "! in the group. enableCollapseButtonWhenEmpty - determines if the collapse/expand
    "! button for an empty group is displayed. showEmptyGroup - determines if the
    "! header/footer of an empty group is displayed.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter collapsed                    | (boolean) Determines if the group is collapsed or expanded. Default: false.
    "! @parameter auto_priority                | (boolean) Determines if the group will automatically set the priority based
    "!                         on the highest priority of its notifications or get its priority from the
    "!                         priority property. Default: true.
    "! @parameter show_empty_group             | (boolean) Determines if the group header/footer of the empty group will be
    "!                         always shown. By default groups with 0 notifications are not shown.
    "!                         Default: false.
    "! @parameter enable_collapse_button_when_em | (boolean) Determines if the collapse/expand button for an empty group is
    "!                         displayed. Default: false.
    "! @parameter show_items_counter           | (boolean) Determines if the items counter inside the group header will be
    "!                         visible. Note: Counter value represents the number of currently visible
    "!                         (loaded) items inside the group. Default: true.
    "! @parameter priority                     | (sap.ui.core.Priority) Determines the priority of the Notification.
    "!                         Default: None.
    "! @parameter title                        | (string) Determines the title of the NotificationListBase item.
    "! @parameter show_buttons                 | (boolean) Determines the action buttons visibility. Note: Action buttons
    "!                         are not shown when Notification List Groups are collapsed. Default: true.
    "! @parameter show_close_button            | (boolean) Determines the visibility of the close button. Default: true.
    "! @parameter type                         | (sap.m.ListType) Defines the visual indication and behavior of the list
    "!                         items, e.g. Active , Navigation , Detail . Default: Inactive.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder is rendered instead of the real control. Default:
    "!                         true.
    "! @parameter unread                       | (boolean) Activates the unread indicator for the list item, if set to true
    "!                         . Note: This flag is ignored when the showUnread property of the parent is
    "!                         set to false . Default: false.
    "! @parameter selected                     | (boolean) Defines the selected state of the list items. Note: Binding the
    "!                         selected property in single selection modes may cause unwanted results if
    "!                         you have more than one selected items in your binding. Default: false.
    "! @parameter counter                      | (int) Defines the counter value of the list items.
    "! @parameter highlight                    | (string) Defines the highlight state of the list items. Valid values for
    "!                         the highlight property are values of the enumerations
    "!                         sap/ui/core/message/MessageType or sap.ui.core.IndicationColor (only values
    "!                         of Indication01 to Indication10 are supported for accessibility contrast
    "!                         reasons). Accessibility support is provided through the associated
    "!                         highlightText property. If the highlight property is set to a value of
    "!                         sap/ui/core/message/MessageType, the highlightText property does not need
    "!                         to be set because a default text is used. However, the default text can be
    "!                         overridden by setting the highlightText property. In all other cases the
    "!                         highlightText property must be set. Default: None.
    "! @parameter highlight_text               | (string) Defines the semantics of the highlight property for accessibility
    "!                         purposes.
    "! @parameter navigated                    | (boolean) The navigated state of the list item. If set to true , a
    "!                         navigation indicator is displayed at the end of the list item. Note: This
    "!                         property must be set for one list item only. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter on_collapse                  | (event) onCollapse event is called when collapse property value is changed
    "! @parameter close                        | (event) Fired when the close button of the notification is pressed. Note:
    "!                         Pressing the close button doesn't destroy the notification automatically.
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) Fires when the user clicks on the control. Note: This event is not
    "!                         fired when the parent mode is SingleSelectMaster or when the
    "!                         includeItemInSelection property is set to true . If there is an interactive
    "!                         element that handles its own press event then the list item's press event
    "!                         is not fired. Also see sap.m.ListBase attachItemPress.
    "! @parameter detail_press                 | (event) Fires when the user clicks on the detail button of the control.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS notification_list_group
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        collapsed                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        auto_priority                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_empty_group             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enable_collapse_button_when_em TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_items_counter           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        priority                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_buttons                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_close_button            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        type                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        unread                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selected                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        counter                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        highlight                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        highlight_text               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        navigated                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        on_collapse                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        close                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        press                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        detail_press                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        PREFERRED PARAMETER title
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.NotificationListItem</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.NotificationListItem
    "! The NotificationListItem control shows notification to the user. Structure The
    "! notification item holds properties for the following elements: description -
    "! additional detail text. hideShowMoreButton - visibility of the "Show More"
    "! button. truncate - determines if title and description are truncated to the
    "! first two lines (usually needed on mobile devices). For each item you can set
    "! some additional status information about the item processing by adding a
    "! sap.m.MessageStrip to the processingMessage aggregation.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter description                  | (string) Determines the description of the NotificationListItem.
    "! @parameter author_initials              | (string) Defines the displayed author initials.
    "! @parameter truncate                     | (boolean) Determines if the text in the title and the description of the
    "!                         notification are truncated to the first two lines. Default: true.
    "! @parameter hide_show_more_button        | (boolean) Determines if the "Show More" button should be hidden. Default:
    "!                         false.
    "! @parameter author_avatar_color          | (sap.m.AvatarColor) Determines the background color of the avatar of the
    "!                         author. Note: By using background colors from the predefined sets, your
    "!                         colors can later be customized from the Theme Designer. Default: Accent6.
    "! @parameter author_name                  | (string) Determines the notification author name.
    "! @parameter author_picture               | (sap.ui.core.URI) Determines the URL of the notification author picture.
    "! @parameter datetime                     | (string) The time stamp of the notification.
    "! @parameter priority                     | (sap.ui.core.Priority) Determines the priority of the Notification.
    "!                         Default: None.
    "! @parameter title                        | (string) Determines the title of the NotificationListBase item.
    "! @parameter show_buttons                 | (boolean) Determines the action buttons visibility. Note: Action buttons
    "!                         are not shown when Notification List Groups are collapsed. Default: true.
    "! @parameter show_close_button            | (boolean) Determines the visibility of the close button. Default: true.
    "! @parameter type                         | (sap.m.ListType) Defines the visual indication and behavior of the list
    "!                         items, e.g. Active , Navigation , Detail . Default: Inactive.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder is rendered instead of the real control. Default:
    "!                         true.
    "! @parameter unread                       | (boolean) Activates the unread indicator for the list item, if set to true
    "!                         . Note: This flag is ignored when the showUnread property of the parent is
    "!                         set to false . Default: false.
    "! @parameter selected                     | (boolean) Defines the selected state of the list items. Note: Binding the
    "!                         selected property in single selection modes may cause unwanted results if
    "!                         you have more than one selected items in your binding. Default: false.
    "! @parameter counter                      | (int) Defines the counter value of the list items.
    "! @parameter highlight                    | (string) Defines the highlight state of the list items. Valid values for
    "!                         the highlight property are values of the enumerations
    "!                         sap/ui/core/message/MessageType or sap.ui.core.IndicationColor (only values
    "!                         of Indication01 to Indication10 are supported for accessibility contrast
    "!                         reasons). Accessibility support is provided through the associated
    "!                         highlightText property. If the highlight property is set to a value of
    "!                         sap/ui/core/message/MessageType, the highlightText property does not need
    "!                         to be set because a default text is used. However, the default text can be
    "!                         overridden by setting the highlightText property. In all other cases the
    "!                         highlightText property must be set. Default: None.
    "! @parameter highlight_text               | (string) Defines the semantics of the highlight property for accessibility
    "!                         purposes.
    "! @parameter navigated                    | (boolean) The navigated state of the list item. If set to true , a
    "!                         navigation indicator is displayed at the end of the list item. Note: This
    "!                         property must be set for one list item only. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter close                        | (event) Fired when the close button of the notification is pressed. Note:
    "!                         Pressing the close button doesn't destroy the notification automatically.
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) Fires when the user clicks on the control. Note: This event is not
    "!                         fired when the parent mode is SingleSelectMaster or when the
    "!                         includeItemInSelection property is set to true . If there is an interactive
    "!                         element that handles its own press event then the list item's press event
    "!                         is not fired. Also see sap.m.ListBase attachItemPress.
    "! @parameter detail_press                 | (event) Fires when the user clicks on the detail button of the control.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS notification_list_item
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        description                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        author_initials              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        truncate                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        hide_show_more_button        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        author_avatar_color          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        author_name                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        author_picture               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        datetime                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        priority                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_buttons                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_close_button            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        type                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        unread                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selected                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        counter                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        highlight                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        highlight_text               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        navigated                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        close                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        press                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        detail_press                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        PREFERRED PARAMETER title
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.NumericContent</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.NumericContent
    "! Shows numeric values used for example in tiles colored according to their
    "! meaning and displays deviations.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter animate_text_change          | (boolean) If set to true, the change of the value will be animated.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter formatter_value              | (boolean) If set to true, the value parameter contains a numeric value and
    "!                         scale. If set to false (default), the value parameter contains a numeric
    "!                         value only. Default: false.
    "! @parameter icon                         | (sap.ui.core.URI) The icon to be displayed as a graphical element within
    "!                         the control. This can be an image or an icon from the icon font.
    "! @parameter icon_description             | (string) Description of an icon that is used in the tooltip.
    "! @parameter indicator                    | (sap.m.DeviationIndicator) The indicator arrow that shows value deviation.
    "!                         Default: None.
    "! @parameter nullify_value                | (boolean) If set to true, the omitted value property is set to 0. Default:
    "!                         true.
    "! @parameter scale                        | (string) The scaling prefix. Financial characters can be used for
    "!                         currencies and counters. The SI prefixes can be used for units. If the
    "!                         scaling prefix contains more than three characters, only the first three
    "!                         characters are displayed.
    "! @parameter truncate_value_to            | (int) The number of characters of the value property to display. Note If
    "!                         adaptiveFontSize is set to true the default value of this property will
    "!                         vary between languages. If adaptiveFontSize is set to false the default
    "!                         value of this property is 4 .
    "! @parameter value                        | (string) The actual value.
    "! @parameter value_color                  | (sap.m.ValueColor) The semantic color of the value. Default: Neutral.
    "! @parameter width                        | (sap.ui.core.CSSSize) The width of the control. If it is not set, the size
    "!                         of the control is defined by the 'size' property.
    "! @parameter with_margin                  | (boolean) If the value is set to false, the content is adjusted to the
    "!                         whole size of the control. Default: true.
    "! @parameter state                        | (sap.m.LoadState) Indicates the load status. Default: Loaded.
    "! @parameter adaptive_font_size           | (boolean) If set to its default value true this property applies the
    "!                         appropriate font style class based on the language. When set to false the
    "!                         font size will always be large Default: true.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) The event is fired when the user chooses the numeric content.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS numeric_content
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        animate_text_change          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        formatter_value              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon_description             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        indicator                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        nullify_value                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        scale                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        truncate_value_to            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        value                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        value_color                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        width                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        with_margin                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        state                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        adaptive_font_size           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        press                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        PREFERRED PARAMETER value
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.ObjectAttribute</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.ObjectAttribute
    "! The ObjectAttribute control displays a text field that can be normal or active.
    "! The ObjectAttribute fires a press event when the user chooses the active text.
    "! Note: If property active is set to true , only the value of the text property is
    "! styled and acts as a link. In this case the text property must also be set, as
    "! otherwise there will be no link displayed for the user.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter title                        | (string) Defines the ObjectAttribute title.
    "! @parameter text                         | (string) Defines the ObjectAttribute text.
    "! @parameter active                       | (boolean) Indicates if the ObjectAttribute text is selectable for the user.
    "!                         Note: As of version 1.48, only the value of the text property becomes
    "!                         active (styled and acts like a link) as opposed to both the title and text
    "!                         in the previous versions. If you set this property to true , you have to
    "!                         also set the text property. Note: When active property is set to true , and
    "!                         the text direction of the title or the text does not match the text
    "!                         direction of the application, the textDirection property should be set to
    "!                         ensure correct display.
    "! @parameter reactive_area_mode           | (sap.m.ReactiveAreaMode) Defines the size of the reactive area of the link:
    "!                         ReactiveAreaMode.Inline - The link is displayed as part of a sentence.
    "!                         ReactiveAreaMode.Overlay - The link is displayed as an overlay on top of
    "!                         other interactive parts of the page. Note: It is designed to make links
    "!                         easier to activate and helps meet the WCAG 2.2 Target Size requirement. It
    "!                         is applicable only for the SAP Horizon themes. Note: The Reactive area size
    "!                         is sufficiently large to help users avoid accidentally selecting (clicking
    "!                         or tapping) on unintented UI elements. UI elements positioned over other
    "!                         parts of the page may need an invisible active touch area. This will ensure
    "!                         that no elements beneath are activated accidentally when the user tries to
    "!                         interact with the overlay element. Default: Inline.
    "! @parameter text_direction               | (sap.ui.core.TextDirection) Determines the direction of the text. Available
    "!                         options for the text direction are LTR (left-to-right), RTL
    "!                         (right-to-left), or Inherit. By default the control inherits the text
    "!                         direction from its parent control. Default: Inherit.
    "! @parameter aria_has_popup               | (sap.ui.core.aria.HasPopup) Specifies the value of the aria-haspopup
    "!                         attribute If the value is None , the attribute will not be rendered.
    "!                         Otherwise it will be rendered with the selected value. NOTE: Use this
    "!                         property only when an sap.m.ObjectAttribute instance is active and related
    "!                         to a popover/popup. The value needs to be equal to the main/root role of
    "!                         the popup - e.g. dialog, menu or list (examples: if you have dialog ->
    "!                         dialog, if you have menu -> menu; if you have list -> list; if you have
    "!                         dialog containing a list -> dialog). Do not use it, if you open a standard
    "!                         sap.m.Dialog, MessageBox or other type of modal dialogs. Default: None.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) Fires when the user clicks on active text.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS object_attribute
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        text                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        active                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        reactive_area_mode           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        text_direction               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        aria_has_popup               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        press                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        PREFERRED PARAMETER text
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.ObjectHeader</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.ObjectHeader
    "! ObjectHeader is a display control that enables the user to easily identify a
    "! specific object. The object header title is the key identifier of the object and
    "! additional text and icons can be used to further distinguish it from other
    "! objects. Responsive behavior When using the sap.m.ObjectHeader in SAP Quartz
    "! theme, the breakpoints and layout paddings could be automatically determined by
    "! the container's width. To enable this concept and implement responsive padding
    "! to the ObjectHeader control, add the following class:
    "! sapUiResponsivePadding--header .
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter title                        | (string) Determines the title of the ObjectHeader .
    "! @parameter number                       | (string) Determines the displayed number of the ObjectHeader number field.
    "! @parameter number_unit                  | (string) Determines the units qualifier of the ObjectHeader number. Note:
    "!                         The value of the numberUnit is not displayed if the number property is set
    "!                         to null .
    "! @parameter intro                        | (string) Determines the introductory text for the ObjectHeader .
    "! @parameter intro_active                 | (boolean) Determines whether the introductory text of the ObjectHeader is
    "!                         clickable.
    "! @parameter title_active                 | (boolean) Determines whether the title of the ObjectHeader is clickable and
    "!                         is set only if a title is provided.
    "! @parameter icon                         | (sap.ui.core.URI) Defines the icon of the ObjectHeader . Note: Recursive
    "!                         resolution of binding expressions is not supported by the framework. It
    "!                         works only in ObjectHeader, since it is a composite control and creates an
    "!                         Image control internally.
    "! @parameter icon_active                  | (boolean) Determines whether the ObjectHeader icon is clickable.
    "! @parameter icon_alt                     | (string) Determines the alternative text of the ObjectHeader icon. The text
    "!                         is displayed if the image for the icon is not available, or cannot be
    "!                         displayed. Note: Provide an empty string value for the iconAlt property in
    "!                         case you want to use the icon for decoration only.
    "! @parameter icon_tooltip                 | (string) Determines the tooltip text of the ObjectHeader icon.
    "! @parameter icon_density_aware           | (boolean) By default, this is set to true but then one or more requests are
    "!                         sent trying to get the density perfect version of image if this version of
    "!                         image doesn't exist on the server. If bandwidth is the key for the
    "!                         application, set this value to false . Default: true.
    "! @parameter image_shape                  | (sap.m.ObjectHeaderPictureShape) Determines whether the picture should be
    "!                         displayed in a square or with a circle-shaped mask just like in
    "!                         sap.uxap.ObjectPageHeader. Note: This property takes effect only on Images
    "!                         and it is ignored for Icons. Default: Square.
    "! @parameter show_title_selector          | (boolean) Determines whether the selector arrow icon/image is displayed and
    "!                         can be pressed. Default: false.
    "! @parameter number_state                 | (sap.ui.core.ValueState) Determines the value state of the number and
    "!                         numberUnit properties. Default: None.
    "! @parameter condensed                    | (boolean) ObjectHeader with title, one attribute, number, and number unit.
    "!                         Note: Only applied if the responsive property is set to false . Default:
    "!                         false.
    "! @parameter background_design            | (sap.m.BackgroundDesign) Determines the background color of the
    "!                         ObjectHeader . Note: The different types of ObjectHeader come with
    "!                         different default background: non responsive - Transparent responsive -
    "!                         Translucent condensed - Solid
    "! @parameter responsive                   | (boolean) Determines whether the ObjectHeader is rendered with a different
    "!                         design that reacts responsively to the screen sizes. When the responsive
    "!                         property is set to true , the following behavior specifics for the control
    "!                         exist: If an image (or an icon font) is set to the icon property, it is
    "!                         hidden in portrait mode on phone. The title is truncated to 80 characters
    "!                         if longer. For portrait mode on phone, the title is truncated to 50
    "!                         characters. Default: false.
    "! @parameter full_screen_optimized        | (boolean) Optimizes the display of the elements of the ObjectHeader . Set
    "!                         this property to true if your app uses a fullscreen layout (as opposed to a
    "!                         master-detail or other split-screen layout). Note : Only applied if the
    "!                         responsive property is also set to true . If set to true , the following
    "!                         situations apply: On desktop, 1-3 attributes/statuses - positioned as a
    "!                         third block on the right side of the Title/Number group On desktop, 4+
    "!                         attributes/statuses - 4 columns below the Title/Number On tablet (portrait
    "!                         mode), always in 2 columns below the Title/Number On tablet (landscape
    "!                         mode), 1-2 attributes/statuses - 2 columns below the Title/Number On tablet
    "!                         (landscape mode), 3+ attributes/statuses - 3 columns below the Title/Number
    "!                         On phone, the attributes and statuses are always positioned in 1 column
    "!                         below the Title/Number of the ObjectHeader . If set to false , the
    "!                         attributes and statuses are being positioned below the Title/Number of the
    "!                         ObjectHeader in 2 or 3 columns depending on their number: On desktop, 1-4
    "!                         attributes/statuses - 2 columns On desktop, 5+ attributes/statuses - 3
    "!                         columns On tablet, always in 2 columns Default: false.
    "! @parameter title_href                   | (sap.ui.core.URI) Defines the title link target URI. Supports standard
    "!                         hyperlink behavior. Note: If an action should be triggered, this property
    "!                         should not be set, but instead an event handler for the titlePress event
    "!                         should be registered.
    "! @parameter title_target                 | (string) Determines the target attribute for the title link. Options are
    "!                         _self , _top , _blank , _parent , _search . Alternatively, a frame name can
    "!                         be entered.
    "! @parameter intro_href                   | (sap.ui.core.URI) Determines the intro link target URI. Supports standard
    "!                         hyperlink behavior. If an action should be triggered, this should not be
    "!                         set, but instead an event handler for the introPress event should be
    "!                         registered.
    "! @parameter intro_target                 | (string) Determines the target attribute for the intro link. Options are
    "!                         _self , _top , _blank , _parent , _search . Alternatively, a frame name can
    "!                         be entered.
    "! @parameter title_text_direction         | (sap.ui.core.TextDirection) Specifies the title text directionality with
    "!                         enumerated options. By default, the control inherits text direction from
    "!                         the DOM. Default: Inherit.
    "! @parameter intro_text_direction         | (sap.ui.core.TextDirection) Specifies the intro text directionality with
    "!                         enumerated options. By default, the control inherits text direction from
    "!                         the DOM. Default: Inherit.
    "! @parameter number_text_direction        | (sap.ui.core.TextDirection) Specifies the number and unit text
    "!                         directionality with enumerated options. By default, the control inherits
    "!                         text direction from the DOM. Default: Inherit.
    "! @parameter title_selector_tooltip       | (string) Determines a custom text for the tooltip of the select title
    "!                         arrow. If not set, a default text of the tooltip will be displayed.
    "!                         Default: Options.
    "! @parameter title_level                  | (sap.ui.core.TitleLevel) Defines the semantic level of the title. This
    "!                         information is used by assistive technologies, such as screen readers to
    "!                         create a hierarchical site map for faster navigation. Depending on this
    "!                         setting an HTML h1-h6 element is used. Default: H1.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter title_press                  | (event) Event is fired when the title is active and the user taps/clicks on
    "!                         it
    "! @parameter intro_press                  | (event) Event is fired when the intro is active and the user taps/clicks on
    "!                         it
    "! @parameter icon_press                   | (event) Event is fired when the title icon is active and the user
    "!                         taps/clicks on it
    "! @parameter title_selector_press         | (event) Event is fired when the object header title selector (down-arrow)
    "!                         is pressed
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS object_header
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        number                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        number_unit                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        intro                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        intro_active                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title_active                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon_active                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon_alt                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon_tooltip                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon_density_aware           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        image_shape                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_title_selector          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        number_state                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        condensed                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        background_design            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        responsive                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        full_screen_optimized        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title_href                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title_target                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        intro_href                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        intro_target                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title_text_direction         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        intro_text_direction         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        number_text_direction        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title_selector_tooltip       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title_level                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title_press                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        intro_press                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon_press                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title_selector_press         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        PREFERRED PARAMETER title
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.ObjectIdentifier</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.ObjectIdentifier
    "! The ObjectIdentifier is a display control that enables the user to easily
    "! identify a specific object. The ObjectIdentifier title is the key identifier of
    "! the object and additional text can be used to further distinguish it from other
    "! objects. Note: This control should not be used with sap.m.Label or in Forms
    "! along with sap.m.Label.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter title                        | (string) Defines the object title.
    "! @parameter text                         | (string) Defines the object text.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Indicates if the ObjectIdentifier is visible. An invisible
    "!                         ObjectIdentifier is not being rendered. Default: true.
    "! @parameter title_active                 | (boolean) Indicates if the ObjectIdentifier's title is clickable. Default:
    "!                         false.
    "! @parameter reactive_area_mode           | (sap.m.ReactiveAreaMode) Defines the size of the reactive area of the link:
    "!                         ReactiveAreaMode.Inline - The link is displayed as part of a sentence.
    "!                         ReactiveAreaMode.Overlay - The link is displayed as an overlay on top of
    "!                         other interactive parts of the page. Note: It is designed to make links
    "!                         easier to activate and helps meet the WCAG 2.2 Target Size requirement. It
    "!                         is applicable only for the SAP Horizon themes. Note: The Reactive area size
    "!                         is sufficiently large to help users avoid accidentally selecting (clicking
    "!                         or tapping) on unintented UI elements. UI elements positioned over other
    "!                         parts of the page may need an invisible active touch area. This will ensure
    "!                         that no elements beneath are activated accidentally when the user tries to
    "!                         interact with the overlay element. Default: Inline.
    "! @parameter text_direction               | (sap.ui.core.TextDirection) Specifies the element's text directionality
    "!                         with enumerated options. By default, the control inherits text direction
    "!                         from the DOM. Default: Inherit.
    "! @parameter empty_indicator_mode         | (sap.m.EmptyIndicatorMode) Specifies if an empty indicator should be
    "!                         displayed when there is no text. Default: Off.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter title_press                  | (event) Fires when the title is active and the user taps/clicks on it.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS object_identifier
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        text                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title_active                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        reactive_area_mode           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        text_direction               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        empty_indicator_mode         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title_press                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        PREFERRED PARAMETER text
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.ObjectListItem</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.ObjectListItem
    "! ObjectListItem is a display control that provides summary information about an
    "! object as a list item. The ObjectListItem title is the key identifier of the
    "! object. Additional text and icons can be used to further distinguish it from
    "! other objects. Attributes and statuses can be used to provide additional meaning
    "! about the object to the user. Note: The control must only be used in the context
    "! of a list.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter title                        | (string) Defines the ObjectListItem title.
    "! @parameter number                       | (string) Defines the ObjectListItem number.
    "! @parameter number_unit                  | (string) Defines the number units qualifier of the ObjectListItem.
    "! @parameter intro                        | (string) Defines the introductory text for the ObjectListItem.
    "! @parameter icon                         | (sap.ui.core.URI) ObjectListItem icon displayed to the left of the title.
    "! @parameter active_icon                  | (sap.ui.core.URI) Icon displayed when the ObjectListItem is active.
    "! @parameter icon_density_aware           | (boolean) By default, this is set to true but then one or more requests are
    "!                         sent trying to get the density perfect version of image (in case this
    "!                         version of image doesn't exist on the server). If bandwidth is key for the
    "!                         application, set this value to false. Default: true.
    "! @parameter number_state                 | (sap.ui.core.ValueState) Defines the ObjectListItem number and numberUnit
    "!                         value state. Default: None.
    "! @parameter title_text_direction         | (sap.ui.core.TextDirection) Determines the text direction of the item
    "!                         title. Available options for the title direction are LTR (left-to-right)
    "!                         and RTL (right-to-left). By default the item title inherits the text
    "!                         direction from its parent. Default: Inherit.
    "! @parameter intro_text_direction         | (sap.ui.core.TextDirection) Determines the text direction of the item
    "!                         intro. Available options for the intro direction are LTR (left-to-right)
    "!                         and RTL (right-to-left). By default the item intro inherits the text
    "!                         direction from its parent. Default: Inherit.
    "! @parameter number_text_direction        | (sap.ui.core.TextDirection) Determines the text direction of the item
    "!                         number. Available options for the number direction are LTR (left-to-right)
    "!                         and RTL (right-to-left). By default the item number inherits the text
    "!                         direction from its parent. Default: Inherit.
    "! @parameter type                         | (sap.m.ListType) Defines the visual indication and behavior of the list
    "!                         items, e.g. Active , Navigation , Detail . Default: Inactive.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder is rendered instead of the real control. Default:
    "!                         true.
    "! @parameter unread                       | (boolean) Activates the unread indicator for the list item, if set to true
    "!                         . Note: This flag is ignored when the showUnread property of the parent is
    "!                         set to false . Default: false.
    "! @parameter selected                     | (boolean) Defines the selected state of the list items. Note: Binding the
    "!                         selected property in single selection modes may cause unwanted results if
    "!                         you have more than one selected items in your binding. Default: false.
    "! @parameter counter                      | (int) Defines the counter value of the list items.
    "! @parameter highlight                    | (string) Defines the highlight state of the list items. Valid values for
    "!                         the highlight property are values of the enumerations
    "!                         sap/ui/core/message/MessageType or sap.ui.core.IndicationColor (only values
    "!                         of Indication01 to Indication10 are supported for accessibility contrast
    "!                         reasons). Accessibility support is provided through the associated
    "!                         highlightText property. If the highlight property is set to a value of
    "!                         sap/ui/core/message/MessageType, the highlightText property does not need
    "!                         to be set because a default text is used. However, the default text can be
    "!                         overridden by setting the highlightText property. In all other cases the
    "!                         highlightText property must be set. Default: None.
    "! @parameter highlight_text               | (string) Defines the semantics of the highlight property for accessibility
    "!                         purposes.
    "! @parameter navigated                    | (boolean) The navigated state of the list item. If set to true , a
    "!                         navigation indicator is displayed at the end of the list item. Note: This
    "!                         property must be set for one list item only. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) Fires when the user clicks on the control. Note: This event is not
    "!                         fired when the parent mode is SingleSelectMaster or when the
    "!                         includeItemInSelection property is set to true . If there is an interactive
    "!                         element that handles its own press event then the list item's press event
    "!                         is not fired. Also see sap.m.ListBase attachItemPress.
    "! @parameter detail_press                 | (event) Fires when the user clicks on the detail button of the control.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS object_list_item
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        number                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        number_unit                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        intro                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        active_icon                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon_density_aware           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        number_state                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title_text_direction         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        intro_text_direction         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        number_text_direction        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        type                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        unread                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selected                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        counter                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        highlight                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        highlight_text               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        navigated                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        press                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        detail_press                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        PREFERRED PARAMETER title
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.ObjectMarker</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.ObjectMarker
    "! The sap.m.ObjectMarker control represents one of the following predefined types:
    "! Flagged Favorite Draft Locked LockedBy Unsaved UnsavedBy Note : Use the
    "! LockedBy/UnsavedBy type along with the additionalInfo property to display the
    "! name of the user who locked/changed the object. If additionalInfo property is
    "! not set when using LockedBy/UnsavedBy types, the string "Locked by another
    "! user"/"Unsaved changes by another user" will be displayed. If you don't want to
    "! display name of the user, simply use the Locked/Unsaved types.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter type                         | (sap.m.ObjectMarkerType) Sets one of the predefined types. Note : If the
    "!                         visibility property is not specified explicitly, every type comes with
    "!                         predefined one as follows: For Flagged and Favorite the icon is visible and
    "!                         the text is not displayed For Draft the text is visible and the icon is not
    "!                         displayed For Locked , LockedBy , Unsaved and UnsavedBy - on screens larger
    "!                         than 600px both icon and text are visible, otherwise only the icon
    "! @parameter reactive_area_mode           | (sap.m.ReactiveAreaMode) Defines the size of the reactive area of the link:
    "!                         ReactiveAreaMode.Inline - The link is displayed as part of a sentence.
    "!                         ReactiveAreaMode.Overlay - The link is displayed as an overlay on top of
    "!                         other interactive parts of the page. Note: It is designed to make links
    "!                         easier to activate and helps meet the WCAG 2.2 Target Size requirement. It
    "!                         is applicable only for the SAP Horizon themes. Note: The Reactive area size
    "!                         is sufficiently large to help users avoid accidentally selecting (clicking
    "!                         or tapping) on unintented UI elements. UI elements positioned over other
    "!                         parts of the page may need an invisible active touch area. This will ensure
    "!                         that no elements beneath are activated accidentally when the user tries to
    "!                         interact with the overlay element. Default: Inline.
    "! @parameter visibility                   | (sap.m.ObjectMarkerVisibility) Sets one of the visibility states.
    "!                         Visibility states are as follows: IconOnly - displays only icon, regardless
    "!                         of the screen size TextOnly - displays only text, regardless of the screen
    "!                         size IconAndText - displays both icon and text, regardless of the screen
    "!                         size
    "! @parameter additional_info              | (string) Sets additional information to the displayed type . Note: If no
    "!                         type is set, the additional information will not be displayed.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) Event is fired when the ObjectMarker is interactive and the user
    "!                         taps/clicks on it.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS object_marker
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        type                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        reactive_area_mode           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visibility                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        additional_info              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        press                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.ObjectNumber</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.ObjectNumber
    "! The ObjectNumber control displays number and number unit properties for an
    "! object. The number can be displayed using semantic colors to provide additional
    "! meaning about the object to the user. With 1.63, large design of the control is
    "! supported by setting sapMObjectNumberLarge CSS class to the ObjectNumber . With
    "! 1.110, inner text wrapping could be enabled by adding the
    "! sapMObjectNumberLongText CSS class to the ObjectNumber . This class can be added
    "! by using оObjectStatus.addStyleClass("sapMObjectNumberLongText"); Note: To
    "! fulfill the design guidelines when you are using sapMObjectNumberLarge CSS class
    "! set the emphasized property to false .
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter number                       | (string) Defines the number field.
    "! @parameter emphasized                   | (boolean) Indicates if the object number should appear emphasized. Default:
    "!                         true.
    "! @parameter state                        | (sap.ui.core.ValueState) Determines the object number's value state.
    "!                         Setting this state will cause the number to be rendered in state-specific
    "!                         colors. Default: None.
    "! @parameter unit                         | (string) Defines the number units qualifier. If numberUnit and unit are
    "!                         both set, the unit value is used.
    "! @parameter text_direction               | (sap.ui.core.TextDirection) Available options for the number and unit text
    "!                         direction are LTR(left-to-right) and RTL(right-to-left). By default, the
    "!                         control inherits the text direction from its parent control. Default:
    "!                         Inherit.
    "! @parameter text_align                   | (sap.ui.core.TextAlign) Sets the horizontal alignment of the number and
    "!                         unit. Default: Begin.
    "! @parameter active                       | (boolean) Indicates if the ObjectNumber text and icon can be clicked/tapped
    "!                         by the user. Note: If you set this property to true , you have to set also
    "!                         the number or unit property. Default: false.
    "! @parameter reactive_area_mode           | (sap.m.ReactiveAreaMode) Defines the size of the reactive area of the link:
    "!                         ReactiveAreaMode.Inline - The link is displayed as part of a sentence.
    "!                         ReactiveAreaMode.Overlay - The link is displayed as an overlay on top of
    "!                         other interactive parts of the page. Note: It is designed to make links
    "!                         easier to activate and helps meet the WCAG 2.2 Target Size requirement. It
    "!                         is applicable only for the SAP Horizon themes. Note: The Reactive area size
    "!                         is sufficiently large to help users avoid accidentally selecting (clicking
    "!                         or tapping) on unintented UI elements. UI elements positioned over other
    "!                         parts of the page may need an invisible active touch area. This will ensure
    "!                         that no elements beneath are activated accidentally when the user tries to
    "!                         interact with the overlay element. Default: Inline.
    "! @parameter inverted                     | (boolean) Determines whether the background color reflects the set state
    "!                         instead of the control's text. Default: false.
    "! @parameter empty_indicator_mode         | (sap.m.EmptyIndicatorMode) Specifies if an empty indicator should be
    "!                         displayed when there is no number. Default: Off.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) Fires when the user clicks/taps on active Object Number .
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS object_number
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        number                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        emphasized                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        state                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        unit                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        text_direction               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        text_align                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        active                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        reactive_area_mode           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        inverted                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        empty_indicator_mode         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        press                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        PREFERRED PARAMETER state
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.ObjectStatus</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.ObjectStatus
    "! Status information that can be either text with a value state, or an icon.
    "! Wrapping and Truncation Behavior The ObjectStatus usually is a short text.
    "! However, if the text is longer it wraps (word by word). Icon and text can be
    "! separated. Note: It maybe handled differently depending on the individual
    "! control use case. For example in sap.ui.table.Table the text of the control is
    "! truncated. With 1.63, large design of the control is supported by setting
    "! sapMObjectStatusLarge CSS class to the ObjectStatus . With 1.110, Inner text
    "! wrapping could be enabled for longer texts without spaces (such as a serial
    "! number that doesn't fit on one line) by adding sapMObjectStatusLongText CSS
    "! class to the ObjectStatus . This class can be added by using
    "! оObjectStatus.addStyleClass("sapMObjectStatusLongText"); With 1.130, bigger line
    "! height for texts that require it (like Thai) can be enabled by adding
    "! sapUiHigherText CSS class to the ObjectStatus . This class can be added by using
    "! оObjectStatus.addStyleClass("sapUiHigherText");
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter title                        | (string) Defines the ObjectStatus title.
    "! @parameter text                         | (string) Defines the ObjectStatus text.
    "! @parameter active                       | (boolean) Indicates if the ObjectStatus text and icon can be clicked/tapped
    "!                         by the user. Note: If you set this property to true , you have to also set
    "!                         the text or icon property. Default: false.
    "! @parameter reactive_area_mode           | (sap.m.ReactiveAreaMode) Defines the size of the reactive area of the link:
    "!                         ReactiveAreaMode.Inline - The link is displayed as part of a sentence.
    "!                         ReactiveAreaMode.Overlay - The link is displayed as an overlay on top of
    "!                         other interactive parts of the page. Note: It is designed to make links
    "!                         easier to activate and helps meet the WCAG 2.2 Target Size requirement. It
    "!                         is applicable only for the SAP Horizon themes. Note: The Reactive area size
    "!                         is sufficiently large to help users avoid accidentally selecting (clicking
    "!                         or tapping) on unintented UI elements. UI elements positioned over other
    "!                         parts of the page may need an invisible active touch area. This will ensure
    "!                         that no elements beneath are activated accidentally when the user tries to
    "!                         interact with the overlay element. Default: Inline.
    "! @parameter state                        | (string) Defines the text value state. The allowed values are from the enum
    "!                         type sap.ui.core.ValueState . Since version 1.66 the state property also
    "!                         accepts values from enum type sap.ui.core.IndicationColor . Default:
    "!                         sap.ui.core.ValueState.None.
    "! @parameter inverted                     | (boolean) Determines whether the background color reflects the set state
    "!                         instead of the control's text. Default: false.
    "! @parameter icon                         | (sap.ui.core.URI) Icon URI. This may be either an icon font or image path.
    "! @parameter icon_density_aware           | (boolean) By default, this is set to true but then one or more requests are
    "!                         sent trying to get the density perfect version of image if this version of
    "!                         image doesn't exist on the server. If bandwidth is key for the application,
    "!                         set this value to false. Default: true.
    "! @parameter text_direction               | (sap.ui.core.TextDirection) Determines the direction of the text, not
    "!                         including the title. Available options for the text direction are LTR
    "!                         (left-to-right) and RTL (right-to-left). By default the control inherits
    "!                         the text direction from its parent control. Default: Inherit.
    "! @parameter empty_indicator_mode         | (sap.m.EmptyIndicatorMode) Specifies if an empty indicator should be
    "!                         displayed when there is no text. Default: Off.
    "! @parameter state_announcement_text      | (string) Еnables overriding of the default state announcement.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) Fires when the user clicks/taps on active text.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS object_status
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        title                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        text                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        active                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        reactive_area_mode           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        state                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        inverted                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        icon_density_aware           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        text_direction               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        empty_indicator_mode         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        state_announcement_text      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        press                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        PREFERRED PARAMETER text
      RETURNING
