    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.ui.layout.ResponsiveFlowLayoutData</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.ui.layout.ResponsiveFlowLayoutData
    "! This is a LayoutData element that can be added to a control if this control is
    "! used within a ResponsiveFlowLayout.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter min_width                    | (int) Defines the minimal size in px of a ResponsiveFlowLayout element. The
    "!                         element will be shrunk down to this value. Default: 100.
    "! @parameter weight                       | (int) Defines the weight of the element, that influences the resulting
    "!                         width. If there are several elements within a row of the
    "!                         ResponsiveFlowLayout, each element could have another weight. The bigger
    "!                         the weight of a single element, the wider it will be stretched, i.e. a
    "!                         bigger weight results in a larger width. Default: 1.
    "! @parameter linebreak                    | (boolean) If this property is set, the control in which the LayoutData is
    "!                         added, will always cause a line break within the ResponsiveFlowLayout.
    "!                         Default: false.
    "! @parameter margin                       | (boolean) Prevents any margin of the element if set to false. Default:
    "!                         true.
    "! @parameter linebreakable                | (boolean) Shows if an element can be wrapped into a new row. If this value
    "!                         is set to false, the min-width will be set to 0 and the wrapping is up to
    "!                         the previous element. Default: true.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS responsive_flow_layout_data
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        min_width                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        weight                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        linebreak                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        margin                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        linebreakable                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.ui.layout.form.ResponsiveGridLayout</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.ui.layout.form.ResponsiveGridLayout
    "! The ResponsiveGridLayout control renders a Form using a responsive grid.
    "! Internally the Grid control is used for rendering. Using this layout, the Form
    "! is rendered in a responsive way. Depending on the available space, the
    "! FormContainers are rendered in one or different columns and the labels are
    "! rendered in the same row as the fields or above the fields. This behavior can be
    "! influenced by the properties of this layout control. On the FormContainers,
    "! labels and content fields, GridData can be used to change the default rendering.
    "! GridData is not supported for FormElements. Note: If GridData is used, this may
    "! result in a much more complex layout than the default one. This means that in
    "! some cases, the calculation for the other content may not bring the expected
    "! result. In such cases, GridData should be used for all content controls to
    "! disable the default behavior. This control cannot be used stand-alone, it just
    "! renders a Form, so it must be assigned to a Form using the layout aggregation.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter label_span_xl                | (int) Default span for labels in extra large size. Note: If the default
    "!                         value -1 is not overwritten with the meaningful one then the labelSpanL
    "!                         value is used. Default: -1.
    "! @parameter label_span_l                 | (int) Default span for labels in large size. Note: If adjustLabelSpan is
    "!                         set, this property is only used if more than 1 FormContainer is in one
    "!                         line. If only 1 FormContainer is in the line, then the labelSpanM value is
    "!                         used. Default: 4.
    "! @parameter label_span_m                 | (int) Default span for labels in medium size. Note: If adjustLabelSpan is
    "!                         set this property is used for full-size FormContainers. If more than one
    "!                         FormContainer is in one line, labelSpanL is used. Default: 2.
    "! @parameter label_span_s                 | (int) Default span for labels in small size. Default: 12.
    "! @parameter adjust_label_span            | (boolean) If set, the usage of labelSpanL and labelSpanM are dependent on
    "!                         the number of FormContainers in one row. If only one FormContainer is
    "!                         displayed in one row, labelSpanM is used to define the size of the label.
    "!                         This is the same for medium and large Forms . This is done to align the
    "!                         labels on forms where full-size FormContainers and multiple-column rows are
    "!                         used in the same Form (because every FormContainer has its own Grid
    "!                         inside). If not set, the usage of labelSpanL and labelSpanM are dependent
    "!                         on the Form size. The number of FormContainers doesn't matter in this case.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter empty_span_xl                | (int) Number of grid cells that are empty at the end of each line on extra
    "!                         large size. Note: If the default value -1 is not overwritten with the
    "!                         meaningful one then the emptySpanL value is used. Default: -1.
    "! @parameter empty_span_l                 | (int) Number of grid cells that are empty at the end of each line on large
    "!                         size. Default: 0.
    "! @parameter empty_span_m                 | (int) Number of grid cells that are empty at the end of each line on medium
    "!                         size. Default: 0.
    "! @parameter empty_span_s                 | (int) Number of grid cells that are empty at the end of each line on small
    "!                         size. Default: 0.
    "! @parameter columns_xl                   | (int) Number of columns for extra large size. The number of columns for
    "!                         extra large size must not be smaller than the number of columns for large
    "!                         size. Note: If the default value -1 is not overwritten with the meaningful
    "!                         one then the columnsL value is used (from the backward compatibility
    "!                         reasons). Default: -1.
    "! @parameter columns_l                    | (int) Number of columns for large size. The number of columns for large
    "!                         size must not be smaller than the number of columns for medium size.
    "!                         Default: 2.
    "! @parameter columns_m                    | (int) Number of columns for medium size. Default: 1.
    "! @parameter single_container_full_size   | (boolean) If the Form contains only one single FormContainer and this
    "!                         property is set, the FormContainer is displayed using the full size of the
    "!                         Form. In this case the properties columnsXL , columnsL and columnsM are
    "!                         ignored. In all other cases the FormContainer is displayed in the size of
    "!                         one column. Default: true.
    "! @parameter breakpoint_xl                | (int) Breakpoint (in pixel) between large size and extra large (XL) size.
    "!                         Default: 1440.
    "! @parameter breakpoint_l                 | (int) Breakpoint (in pixel) between Medium size and Large size. Default:
    "!                         1024.
    "! @parameter breakpoint_m                 | (int) Breakpoint (in pixel) between Small size and Medium size. Default:
    "!                         600.
    "! @parameter background_design            | (sap.ui.layout.BackgroundDesign) Specifies the background color of the Form
    "!                         content. Note: The visualization of the different options depends on the
    "!                         theme used. Default: Translucent.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS responsive_grid_layout
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        label_span_xl                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        label_span_l                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        label_span_m                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        label_span_s                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        adjust_label_span            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        empty_span_xl                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        empty_span_l                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        empty_span_m                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        empty_span_s                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        columns_xl                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        columns_l                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        columns_m                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        single_container_full_size   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        breakpoint_xl                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        breakpoint_l                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        breakpoint_m                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        background_design            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.ui.layout.form.ResponsiveLayout</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.ui.layout.form.ResponsiveLayout
    "! The ResponsiveLayout renders a Form with a responsive layout. Internally the
    "! ResponsiveFlowLayout is used. The responsiveness of this layout tries to best
    "! use the available space. This means that the order of the FormContainers ,
    "! labels and fields depends on the available space. On the FormContainers ,
    "! FormElements , labels and content fields, ResponsiveFlowLayoutData can be used
    "! to change the default rendering. We suggest using the ResponsiveGridLayout
    "! instead of this layout because this is easier to consume and brings more stable
    "! responsive output. Note: If ResponsiveFlowLayoutData are used this may result in
    "! a much more complex layout than the default one. This means that in some cases,
    "! the calculation for the other content may not bring the expected result. In such
    "! cases, ResponsiveFlowLayoutData should be used for all content controls to
    "! disable the default behavior. This control cannot be used stand-alone, it just
    "! renders a Form , so it must be assigned to a Form using the layout aggregation.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter background_design            | (sap.ui.layout.BackgroundDesign) Specifies the background color of the Form
    "!                         content. Note: The visualization of the different options depends on the
    "!                         theme used. Default: Translucent.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
