    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.ResponsivePopover</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.ResponsivePopover
    "! Overview The responsive popover acts as a popover on desktop and tablet, while
    "! on phone it acts as a dialog with stretch set to true. Note: It is recommended
    "! that ResponsivePopover is used in fragments otherwise there might be some
    "! implications on the user experience. For example, on desktop, open or close
    "! functions of the Popover might not be called. Usage When you want to make sure
    "! that all content is visible on any device.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter placement                    | (sap.m.PlacementType) This property only takes effect on desktop or tablet.
    "!                         Please see the documentation sap.m.Popover placement. Default: Right.
    "! @parameter show_header                  | (boolean) This property is supported by both variants. Please see the
    "!                         documentation on sap.m.Popover showHeader and sap.m.Dialog showHeader
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter title                        | (string) This property is supported by both variants. Please see the
    "!                         documentation on sap.m.Popover title and sap.m.Dialog title
    "! @parameter icon                         | (sap.ui.core.URI) This property only takes effect on phone. Please see the
    "!                         documentation sap.m.Dialog icon.
    "! @parameter modal                        | (boolean) This property only takes effect on desktop or tablet. Please see
    "!                         the documentation sap.m.Popover modal.
    "! @parameter offset_x                     | (int) This property only takes effect on desktop or tablet. Please see the
    "!                         documentation sap.m.Popover offsetX.
    "! @parameter offset_y                     | (int) This property only takes effect on desktop or tablet. Please see the
    "!                         documentation sap.m.Popover offsetY.
    "! @parameter show_arrow                   | (boolean) This property only takes effect on desktop or tablet. Please see
    "!                         the documentation sap.m.Popover showArrow. Default: true.
    "! @parameter content_width                | (sap.ui.core.CSSSize) This property is supported by both variants. Please
    "!                         see the documentation on sap.m.Popover contentWidth and sap.m.Dialog
    "!                         contentWidth
    "! @parameter content_height               | (sap.ui.core.CSSSize) This property is supported by both variants. Please
    "!                         see the documentation on sap.m.Popover contentHeight and sap.m.Dialog
    "!                         contentHeight
    "! @parameter horizontal_scrolling         | (boolean) This property is supported by both variants. Please see the
    "!                         documentation on sap.m.Popover horizontalScrolling and sap.m.Dialog
    "!                         horizontalScrolling Default: true.
    "! @parameter vertical_scrolling           | (boolean) This property is supported by both variants. Please see the
    "!                         documentation on sap.m.Popover verticalScrolling and sap.m.Dialog
    "!                         verticalScrolling Default: true.
    "! @parameter show_close_button            | (boolean) Determines if a close button should be inserted into the dialog's
    "!                         header dynamically to close the dialog. This property only takes effect on
    "!                         phone. Note: The close button could be placed only in a sap.m.Bar if a
    "!                         sap.m.Toolbar is passed as a header - the property will not take effect.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter resizable                    | (boolean) Whether resize option is enabled. Default: false.
    "! @parameter title_alignment              | (sap.m.TitleAlignment) Specifies the Title alignment (theme specific). If
    "!                         set to TitleAlignment.Auto , the Title will be aligned as it is set in the
    "!                         theme (if not set, the default value is center ); Other possible values are
    "!                         TitleAlignment.Start (left or right depending on LTR/RTL), and
    "!                         TitleAlignment.Center (centered) Default: Auto.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter before_open                  | (event) Event is fired before popover or dialog is open.
    "! @parameter after_open                   | (event) Event is fired after popover or dialog is open.
    "! @parameter before_close                 | (event) Event is fired before popover or dialog is closed.
    "! @parameter after_close                  | (event) Event is fired after popover or dialog is closed.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS responsive_popover
      IMPORTING
