    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.SegmentedButton</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.SegmentedButton
    "! A horizontal control made of multiple buttons, which can display a title or an
    "! image. Overview The SegmentedButton shows a group of buttons. When the user
    "! clicks or taps one of the buttons, it stays in a pressed state. It automatically
    "! resizes the buttons to fit proportionally within the control. When no width is
    "! set, the control uses the available width.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter width                        | (sap.ui.core.CSSSize) Defines the width of the SegmentedButton control. If
    "!                         not set, it uses the minimum required width to make all buttons inside of
    "!                         the same size (based on the biggest button). Note: This property functions
    "!                         only when the contentMode is set to EqualSized.
    "! @parameter enabled                      | (boolean) Disables all the buttons in the SegmentedButton control. When
    "!                         disabled all the buttons look grey and you cannot focus or click on them.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter selected_key                 | (string) Key of the selected item. If no item to this key is found in the
    "!                         items aggregation, no changes will apply. Only the items aggregation is
    "!                         affected. If duplicate keys exist, the first item matching the key is used.
    "! @parameter content_mode                 | (sap.m.SegmentedButtonContentMode) Defines how the content of the
    "!                         SegmentedButton is sized. Possible values: ContentFit : Each button is
    "!                         sized according to its content. EqualSized : All buttons have equal width,
    "!                         regardless of their content. Default: EqualSized.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter selection_change             | (event) Fires when the user selects an item, which returns the item object.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS segmented_button
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        width                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enabled                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selected_key                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        content_mode                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selection_change             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.SegmentedButtonItem</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.SegmentedButtonItem
    "! Used for creating buttons for the sap.m.SegmentedButton. It is derived from the
    "! sap.ui.core.Item.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter icon                         | (string) The icon, which belongs to the button. This can be a URI to an
    "!                         image or an icon font URI.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the button should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder is rendered instead of the real button. Default: true.
    "! @parameter width                        | (sap.ui.core.CSSSize) Sets the width of the buttons Note: This property
    "!                         functions only when the contentMode is set to EqualSized.
    "! @parameter text                         | (string) The text to be displayed for the item.
    "! @parameter enabled                      | (boolean) Enabled items can be selected. Default: true.
    "! @parameter text_direction               | (sap.ui.core.TextDirection) Options are RTL and LTR. Alternatively, an item
    "!                         can inherit its text direction from its parent control. Default: Inherit.
    "! @parameter key                          | (string) Can be used as input for subsequent actions.
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) Fires when the user clicks on an individual button.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
