    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.Tree</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.Tree
    "! The Tree control provides a tree structure for displaying data in a hierarchy.
    "! Note: Growing feature is not supported by Tree .
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter inset                        | (boolean) Defines the indentation of the container. Setting it to true
    "!                         indents the list. Default: false.
    "! @parameter header_text                  | (string) Defines the header text that appears in the control. Note: If the
    "!                         headerToolbar aggregation is set, then this property is ignored. If this is
    "!                         the case, use, for example, a sap.m.Title control in the toolbar to define
    "!                         a header.
    "! @parameter header_level                 | (sap.ui.core.TitleLevel) Defines the semantic header level of the header
    "!                         text (see headerText property ). This information is, for example, used by
    "!                         assistive technologies, such as screenreaders, to create a hierarchical
    "!                         site map for faster navigation. Depending on this setting, either the ARIA
    "!                         equivalent of an HTML h1-h6 element is used or, when using the Auto level,
    "!                         no explicit level information is used. Note: If the headerToolbar
    "!                         aggregation is set, then this property is ignored. If this is the case,
    "!                         use, for example, a sap.m.Title control in the toolbar to define a header.
    "!                         Default: Auto.
    "! @parameter footer_text                  | (string) Defines the footer text that appears in the control.
    "! @parameter mode                         | (sap.m.ListMode) Defines the mode of the control (e.g. None , SingleSelect
    "!                         , MultiSelect , Delete ). Default: None.
    "! @parameter width                        | (sap.ui.core.CSSSize) Sets the width of the control. Default: 100%.
    "! @parameter include_item_in_selection    | (boolean) Defines whether the items are selectable by clicking on the item
    "!                         itself ( true ) rather than having to set the selection control first.
    "!                         Note: The SingleSelectMaster mode also provides this functionality by
    "!                         default. Default: false.
    "! @parameter show_unread                  | (boolean) Activates the unread indicator for all items, if set to true .
    "!                         Default: false.
    "! @parameter no_data_text                 | (string) This text is displayed if the control contains no items. Note: If
    "!                         both a noDataText property and a noData aggregation are provided, the
    "!                         noData aggregation takes priority. If the noData aggregation is undefined
    "!                         or set to null, the noDataText property is used instead.
    "! @parameter show_no_data                 | (boolean) Defines whether or not the text specified in the noDataText
    "!                         property is displayed. Default: true.
    "! @parameter enable_busy_indicator        | (boolean) When this property is set to true , the control will
    "!                         automatically display a busy indicator when it detects that data is being
    "!                         loaded. This busy indicator blocks the interaction with the items until
    "!                         data loading is finished. By default, the busy indicator will be shown
    "!                         after one second. This behavior can be customized by setting the
    "!                         busyIndicatorDelay property. Default: true.
    "! @parameter mode_animation_on            | (boolean) Defines if animations will be shown while switching between
    "!                         modes. Default: true.
    "! @parameter show_separators              | (sap.m.ListSeparators) Defines which item separator style will be used.
    "!                         Default: All.
    "! @parameter swipe_direction              | (sap.m.SwipeDirection) Defines the direction of the swipe movement (e.g
    "!                         LeftToRight, RightToLeft, Both) to display the control defined in the
    "!                         swipeContent aggregation. Default: Both.
    "! @parameter growing                      | (boolean) If set to true , enables the growing feature of the control to
    "!                         load more items by requesting from the model. Note: : This feature only
    "!                         works when an items aggregation is bound. Growing must not be used together
    "!                         with two-way binding. Default: false.
    "! @parameter growing_threshold            | (int) Defines the number of items to be requested from the model for each
    "!                         grow. This property can only be used if the growing property is set to true
    "!                         . Default: 20.
    "! @parameter growing_trigger_text         | (string) Defines the text displayed on the growing button. The default is a
    "!                         translated text ("More") coming from the message bundle. This property can
    "!                         only be used if the growing property is set to true .
    "! @parameter growing_scroll_to_load       | (boolean) If set to true, the user can scroll down/up to load more items.
    "!                         Otherwise a growing button is displayed at the bottom/top of the control.
    "!                         Note: This property can only be used if the growing property is set to true
    "!                         and only if there is one instance of sap.m.List or sap.m.Table inside the
    "!                         scrollable scroll container (e.g sap.m.Page ). Default: false.
    "! @parameter growing_direction            | (sap.m.ListGrowingDirection) Defines the direction of the growing feature.
    "!                         If set to Downwards the user has to scroll down to load more items or the
    "!                         growing button is displayed at the bottom. If set to Upwards the user has
    "!                         to scroll up to load more items or the growing button is displayed at the
    "!                         top. Default: Downwards.
    "! @parameter remember_selections          | (boolean) If set to true, this control remembers and retains the selection
    "!                         of the items after a binding update has been performed (e.g. sorting,
    "!                         filtering). Note: This feature works only if two-way data binding for the
    "!                         selected property of the item is not used. It also needs to be turned off
    "!                         if the binding context of the item does not always point to the same entry
    "!                         in the model, for example, if the order of the data in the JSONModel is
    "!                         changed. Note: This feature leverages the built-in selection mechanism of
    "!                         the corresponding binding context if the OData V4 model is used. Therefore,
    "!                         all binding-relevant limitations apply in this context as well. For more
    "!                         details, see the setSelected, the bindList, and the requestValueListInfo
    "!                         API documentation. Do not enable this feature if $$sharedRequest or
    "!                         $$clearSelectionOnFilter is active. Note: If this property is set to false
    "!                         , a possible binding context update of items (for example, filtering or
    "!                         sorting the list binding) would clear the selection of the items. Default:
    "!                         true.
    "! @parameter keyboard_mode                | (sap.m.ListKeyboardMode) Defines keyboard handling behavior of the control.
    "!                         Default: Navigation.
    "! @parameter sticky                       | (sap.m.Sticky[]) Defines the section of the control that remains fixed at
    "!                         the top of the page during vertical scrolling as long as the control is in
    "!                         the viewport. Note: Enabling sticky column headers in List controls will
    "!                         not have any effect. There are some known restrictions. A few are given
    "!                         below: If the control is placed in layout containers that have the
    "!                         overflow: hidden or overflow: auto style definition, this can prevent the
    "!                         sticky elements of the control from becoming fixed at the top of the
    "!                         viewport. If sticky column headers are enabled in the sap.m.Table control,
    "!                         setting focus on the column headers will let the table scroll to the top. A
    "!                         transparent toolbar design is not supported for sticky bars. The toolbar
    "!                         will automatically get an intransparent background color. This feature
    "!                         supports only the default height of the toolbar control and the column
    "!                         headers. When sticky group headers are enabled, wrapping in the column
    "!                         headers is not supported.
    "! @parameter multi_select_mode            | (sap.m.MultiSelectMode) Defines the multi-selection mode for the control.
    "!                         If the property is set to ClearAll , then selecting items via the keyboard
    "!                         shortcut CTRL + A and via the selectAll method is not possible. See
    "!                         selectAll for more details. A selection of multiple items is still possible
    "!                         using the range selection feature. For more information about the range
    "!                         selection, see Keyboard Handling for Item Selection. Only relevant for
    "!                         sap.m.Table : If ClearAll is set, the table renders a Deselect All icon in
    "!                         the column header, otherwise a Select All checkbox is shown. The Select All
    "!                         checkbox allows the user to select all the items in the control, and the
    "!                         Deselect All icon deselects the items. Note: This property must be used
    "!                         with the MultiSelect mode. Default: Default.
    "! @parameter item_action_count            | (int) Defines the maximum number of actions displayed for the items. If the
    "!                         number of item actions exceeds the itemActionCount property value, an
    "!                         overflow button will appear, providing access to the additional actions.
    "!                         Note: Only values between 0-2 enables the use of the new actions
    "!                         aggregation. When enabled, the Delete mode and the Detail list item type
    "!                         have no effect. Instead, dedicated actions of type Delete or Edit should be
    "!                         used. Note: As of version 1.147, items with type Navigation render the
    "!                         navigation indicator as an action, which is not counted in itemActionCount
    "!                         . Default: -1.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter toggle_open_state            | (event) Fired when an item has been expanded or collapsed by user
    "!                         interaction.
    "! @parameter selection_change             | (event) Fires when selection is changed via user interaction inside the
    "!                         control.
    "! @parameter delete                       | (event) Fires when delete icon is pressed by user.
    "! @parameter swipe                        | (event) Fires after user's swipe action and before the swipeContent is
    "!                         shown. On the swipe event handler, swipeContent can be changed according to
    "!                         the swiped item. Calling the preventDefault method of the event cancels the
    "!                         swipe action. Note: There is no accessible alternative provided by the
    "!                         control for swiping. Applications that use this functionality must provide
    "!                         an accessible alternative UI to perform the same action.
    "! @parameter update_started               | (event) Fires before items binding is updated (e.g. sorting, filtering)
    "!                         Note: Event handler should not invalidate the control.
    "! @parameter update_finished              | (event) Fires after items binding is updated and processed by the control.
    "! @parameter item_press                   | (event) Fires when an item is pressed unless the item's type property is
    "!                         Inactive .
    "! @parameter before_open_context_menu     | (event) Fired when the context menu is opened. When the context menu is
    "!                         opened, the binding context of the item is set to the given contextMenu .
    "! @parameter item_action_press            | (event) Fired when an item action is pressed.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS tree
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        inset                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        header_text                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        header_level                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        footer_text                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        mode                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        width                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        include_item_in_selection    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_unread                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        no_data_text                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_no_data                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enable_busy_indicator        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        mode_animation_on            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_separators              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        swipe_direction              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing_threshold            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing_trigger_text         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing_scroll_to_load       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        growing_direction            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        remember_selections          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        keyboard_mode                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        sticky                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        multi_select_mode            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        item_action_count            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        toggle_open_state            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selection_change             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        delete                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        swipe                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        update_started               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        update_finished              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        item_press                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        before_open_context_menu     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        item_action_press            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        PREFERRED PARAMETER header_text
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.TreeItemBase</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.TreeItemBase
    "! The sap.m.TreeItemBase contains the basic features of all specific tree items.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter type                         | (sap.m.ListType) Defines the visual indication and behavior of the list
    "!                         items, e.g. Active , Navigation , Detail . Default: Inactive.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder is rendered instead of the real control. Default:
    "!                         true.
    "! @parameter unread                       | (boolean) Activates the unread indicator for the list item, if set to true
    "!                         . Note: This flag is ignored when the showUnread property of the parent is
    "!                         set to false . Default: false.
    "! @parameter selected                     | (boolean) Defines the selected state of the list items. Note: Binding the
    "!                         selected property in single selection modes may cause unwanted results if
    "!                         you have more than one selected items in your binding. Default: false.
    "! @parameter counter                      | (int) Defines the counter value of the list items.
    "! @parameter highlight                    | (string) Defines the highlight state of the list items. Valid values for
    "!                         the highlight property are values of the enumerations
    "!                         sap/ui/core/message/MessageType or sap.ui.core.IndicationColor (only values
    "!                         of Indication01 to Indication10 are supported for accessibility contrast
    "!                         reasons). Accessibility support is provided through the associated
    "!                         highlightText property. If the highlight property is set to a value of
    "!                         sap/ui/core/message/MessageType, the highlightText property does not need
    "!                         to be set because a default text is used. However, the default text can be
    "!                         overridden by setting the highlightText property. In all other cases the
    "!                         highlightText property must be set. Default: None.
    "! @parameter highlight_text               | (string) Defines the semantics of the highlight property for accessibility
    "!                         purposes.
    "! @parameter navigated                    | (boolean) The navigated state of the list item. If set to true , a
    "!                         navigation indicator is displayed at the end of the list item. Note: This
    "!                         property must be set for one list item only. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) Fires when the user clicks on the control. Note: This event is not
    "!                         fired when the parent mode is SingleSelectMaster or when the
    "!                         includeItemInSelection property is set to true . If there is an interactive
    "!                         element that handles its own press event then the list item's press event
    "!                         is not fired. Also see sap.m.ListBase attachItemPress.
    "! @parameter detail_press                 | (event) Fires when the user clicks on the detail button of the control.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS tree_item_base
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        type                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        unread                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selected                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        counter                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        highlight                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        highlight_text               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        navigated                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        press                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        detail_press                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.ui.table.TreeTable</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.ui.table.TreeTable
    "! The TreeTable control provides a comprehensive set of features to display
    "! hierarchical data. The control can be used in combination with JSONModel and
    "! ODataModel V2. For a tree-table-like behavior with OData V4 services, use the
    "! Table control with the ODataV4Hierarchy plugin.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter use_group_mode               | (boolean) If group mode is enabled nodes with subitems are rendered as if
    "!                         they were group headers. This can be used to do the grouping for an OData
    "!                         service on the backend and visualize this in a table. Default: false.
    "! @parameter group_header_property        | (string) The property name of the rows data which will be displayed as a
    "!                         group header if the group mode is enabled
    "! @parameter width                        | (sap.ui.core.CSSSize) Width of the Table. Default: auto.
    "! @parameter column_header_height         | (int) Header row height in pixel. If a value greater than 0 is set, it
    "!                         overrides the height defined in the rowHeight property for the rows in the
    "!                         table's header. The value defines the minimum height, but it cannot be less
    "!                         than the default height based on the content density configuration. The
    "!                         actual height can increase based on the content. Note : In a MultiLabel
    "!                         scenario, the height is applied to each individual row of the table's
    "!                         header.
    "! @parameter column_header_visible        | (boolean) Flag whether the column header is visible or not. Caution: Please
    "!                         be aware that when setting this property to false , a 100% accessibility of
    "!                         the table can't be guaranteed any more. Default: true.
    "! @parameter first_visible_row            | (int) First visible row. Default: 0.
    "! @parameter selection_mode               | (sap.ui.table.SelectionMode) Selection mode of the Table. This property
    "!                         controls whether single or multiple rows can be selected and how the
    "!                         selection can be extended. It may also influence the visual appearance.
    "!                         When the selection mode is changed, the current selection is removed. Note:
    "!                         Since the group header visualization relies on the row selectors, the row
    "!                         selectors are always shown if the grouping functionality (depends on table
    "!                         type) is enabled, even if sap.ui.table.SelectionMode.None is set. Note: The
    "!                         built-in selection API has limited functionality, especially when it is
    "!                         combined with paging (e.g. OData). Therefore, it is recommended to use a
    "!                         selection plugin instead. Note: If a selection plugin is used with the
    "!                         table, the selection mode is controlled by the plugin. Default:
    "!                         MultiToggle.
    "! @parameter selection_behavior           | (sap.ui.table.SelectionBehavior) Selection behavior of the Table. This
    "!                         property defines whether the row selector is displayed and whether the row,
    "!                         the row selector or both can be clicked to select a row. Note: Since the
    "!                         group header visualization relies on the row selectors, the row selectors
    "!                         are always shown if the grouping functionality (depends on table type) is
    "!                         enabled, even if sap.ui.table.SelectionBehavior.RowOnly is set. Default:
    "!                         RowSelector.
    "! @parameter threshold                    | (int) Defines how many additional (not yet visible) data records from the
    "!                         back-end system are pre-fetched to enable smooth scrolling. The threshold
    "!                         is always added to the number of rows. If the number of rows is 10 and the
    "!                         threshold is 100, 110 records will be fetched with the initial load. This
    "!                         property affects requests triggered by changes in the binding, for example,
    "!                         initial loading, sorting, filtering, etc. The threshold that is applied
    "!                         during scrolling can be configured with the scrollThreshold property. If
    "!                         the threshold is lower than the number of rows in the scrollable area (
    "!                         visibleRowCount minus number of fixed rows), this number is used as the
    "!                         threshold . If the value is 0, thresholding is disabled. Default: 100.
    "! @parameter scroll_threshold             | (int) Defines how many additional data records are requested from the
    "!                         back-end system when the user scrolls vertically in the table. The
    "!                         scrollThreshold is always added to the number of rows. If the number of
    "!                         rows is 10 and the scrollThreshold is 100, 110 records will be fetched
    "!                         during scrolling. The threshold that is applied to requests that are not
    "!                         initiated by scrolling can be configured with the threshold property. If
    "!                         the scrollThreshold is lower than the number of rows in the scrollable area
    "!                         (number of rows minus number of fixed rows), this number is used as the
    "!                         scrollThreshold . If the value is 0, no threshold is applied during
    "!                         scrolling. The value -1 applies the same value as the threshold property.
    "!                         Note: This property only takes effect if it is set to a positive integer
    "!                         value. The value of the scrollThreshold should be higher than the threshold
    "!                         value to avoid unnecessary requests. For AnalyticalTable and TreeTable ,
    "!                         the scrollThreshold property must be higher than the threshold property to
    "!                         take effect. Default: -1.
    "! @parameter enable_column_reordering     | (boolean) Flag to enable or disable column reordering Note : Column
    "!                         reordering is possible via drag&drop and keyboard shortcuts. Single-pointer
    "!                         alternative is not provided out-of-the-box and should be implemented on
    "!                         application side. For example the sap.m.p13n.Engine can be used, see the
    "!                         following sample: Personalization for grid table. Default: true.
    "! @parameter show_no_data                 | (boolean) Flag whether to show the no data overlay or not once the table is
    "!                         empty. If set to false the table will just show a grid of empty cells
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter fixed_column_count           | (int) Number of columns that are fixed on the left. Only columns which are
    "!                         not fixed can be scrolled horizontally. Note Fixed columns need a defined
    "!                         width for the feature to work. The aggregated width of all fixed columns
    "!                         must not exceed the table width. Otherwise the table ignores the value of
    "!                         the property and adapts the behavior in an appropriate way to ensure that
    "!                         the user is still able to scroll horizontally. Default: 0.
    "! @parameter enable_column_freeze         | (boolean) Flag whether to show or hide the column menu item to freeze or
    "!                         unfreeze a column. Default: false.
    "! @parameter enable_cell_filter           | (boolean) Flag whether to enable or disable the context menu on cells to
    "!                         trigger a filtering with the cell value. Default: false.
    "! @parameter show_overlay                 | (boolean) Setting this property to true will show an overlay on top of the
    "!                         Table content and users cannot click anymore on the Table content. Default:
    "!                         false.
    "! @parameter enable_select_all            | (boolean) Specifies if a select all button should be displayed in the top
    "!                         left corner. This button is only displayed if the row selector is visible
    "!                         and the selection mode is set to any kind of multi selection. Default:
    "!                         true.
    "! @parameter enable_custom_filter         | (boolean) Set this parameter to true to implement your own filter
    "!                         behaviour. Instead of the filter input box a button will be rendered for
    "!                         which' press event (customFilter) you can register an event handler.
    "!                         Default: false.
    "! @parameter enable_busy_indicator        | (boolean) If set to true , the table changes its busy state, resulting in
    "!                         showing or hiding the busy indicator. The table will switch to busy as soon
    "!                         as data is retrieved to be displayed in the currently visible rows. This
    "!                         happens, for example, during scrolling, filtering, or sorting. As soon as
    "!                         the data has been retrieved, the table switches back to not busy. The busy
    "!                         state of the table can still be set manually by calling sap.ui.core.Control
    "!                         setBusy. Default: false.
    "! @parameter row_action_count             | (int) Number of row actions made visible, hence this property also
    "!                         determines the width of the row action column. The maximum number of
    "!                         visible row actions is 3. If the rowActionTemplate contains more
    "!                         rowActionItems , they are shown in an overflow menu. Default: 0.
    "! @parameter alternate_row_colors         | (boolean) Enables alternating table row colors. Alternate row coloring is
    "!                         not available for the tree mode. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter toggle_open_state            | (event) Fired when a row has been expanded or collapsed by user
    "!                         interaction. Only available in hierarchical mode.
    "! @parameter row_selection_change         | (event) Fired if the row selection of the table has been changed. The event
    "!                         parameters can be used to determine selection changes. To find the selected
    "!                         rows, you should use sap.ui.table.Table getSelectedIndices or the related
    "!                         function of the used selection plugin if it exists. Note: The built-in
    "!                         selection API has limited functionality, especially when it is combined
    "!                         with paging (e.g. OData). Therefore, it is recommended to use a selection
    "!                         plugin instead. Note: If a selection plugin is used with the table, this
    "!                         event won't be fired.
    "! @parameter column_resize                | (event) fired when a table column is resized.
    "! @parameter column_move                  | (event) fired when a table column is moved.
    "! @parameter sort                         | (event) This event is fired before a sort order is applied to a column, if
    "!                         the table is sorted via sap.ui.table.Table sort call or user interaction
    "!                         with the column header. Sorters that are directly applied to the table
    "!                         binding will not fire this event.
    "! @parameter filter                       | (event) This event is fired before a filter is applied to a column, if the
    "!                         table is filtered via sap.ui.table.Table filter call or user interaction
    "!                         with the column header. Filters that are directly applied to the table
    "!                         binding will not fire this event.
    "! @parameter cell_click                   | (event) fired when the user clicks a cell of the table (experimental!).
    "! @parameter before_open_context_menu     | (event) Fired when the context menu is opened. When the context menu is
    "!                         opened, the binding context of the row is set to the context menu.
    "! @parameter column_freeze                | (event) fired when a column of the table should be freezed
    "! @parameter custom_filter                | (event) This event is triggered when the custom filter item of the column
    "!                         menu is pressed. The column on which the event was triggered is passed as
    "!                         parameter.
    "! @parameter paste                        | (event) This event gets fired when the user pastes content from the
    "!                         clipboard to the table. Pasting can be done with the standard keyboard
    "!                         shortcut, if the focus is inside the table.
    "! @parameter rows_updated                 | (event) This event is fired after the table rows have been updated due to
    "!                         rendering, a model update, or a user interaction, for example. Note : This
    "!                         event is fired often and must not be used for performance-critical tasks.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS tree_table
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        use_group_mode               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        group_header_property        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        width                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        column_header_height         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        column_header_visible        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        first_visible_row            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selection_mode               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selection_behavior           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        threshold                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        scroll_threshold             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enable_column_reordering     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_no_data                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        fixed_column_count           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enable_column_freeze         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enable_cell_filter           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_overlay                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enable_select_all            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enable_custom_filter         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enable_busy_indicator        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        row_action_count             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        alternate_row_colors         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        toggle_open_state            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        row_selection_change         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        column_resize                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        column_move                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        sort                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        filter                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        cell_click                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        before_open_context_menu     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        column_freeze                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        custom_filter                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        paste                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        rows_updated                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.UploadCollection</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.UploadCollection
    "! This control allows you to upload single or multiple files from your devices
    "! (desktop, tablet or phone) and attach them to the application. The consuming
    "! application needs to take into account that the consistency checks of the model
    "! during the upload of the file need to be performed, for example, if the user is
    "! editing or deleting a file. As of version 1.63, there is an
    "! sap.m.upload.UploadSet control available that is based on this control.
    "! sap.m.upload.UploadSet provides enhanced handling of headers and requests,
    "! unified behavior of instant and deferred uploads, as well as improved progress
    "! indication.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter file_type                    | (string[]) Defines the allowed file types for the upload. The chosen files
    "!                         will be checked against an array of file types. If at least one file does
    "!                         not fit the file type requirements, the upload is prevented. Example:
    "!                         ["jpg", "png", "bmp"].
    "! @parameter maximum_filename_length      | (int) Specifies the maximum length of a file name. If the maximum file name
    "!                         length is exceeded, the corresponding event 'filenameLengthExceed' is
    "!                         triggered.
    "! @parameter maximum_file_size            | (float) Specifies a file size limit in megabytes that prevents the upload
    "!                         if at least one file exceeds the limit. This property is not supported by
    "!                         Internet Explorer 8 and 9.
    "! @parameter mime_type                    | (string[]) Defines the allowed MIME types of files to be uploaded. The
    "!                         chosen files will be checked against an array of MIME types. If at least
    "!                         one file does not fit the MIME type requirements, the upload is prevented.
    "!                         This property is not supported by Internet Explorer 8 and 9. Example:
    "!                         mimeType ["image/png", "image/jpeg"].
    "! @parameter multiple                     | (boolean) Lets the user select multiple files from the same folder and then
    "!                         upload them. Internet Explorer 8 and 9 do not support this property. Please
    "!                         note that the various operating systems for mobile devices can react
    "!                         differently to the property so that fewer upload functions may be available
    "!                         in some cases. If multiple property is set to false, the control shows an
    "!                         error message if more than one file is chosen for drag & drop. Default:
    "!                         false.
    "! @parameter no_data_text                 | (string) Allows you to set your own text for the 'No data' text label.
    "! @parameter no_data_description          | (string) Allows you to set your own text for the 'No data' description
    "!                         label.
    "! @parameter same_filename_allowed        | (boolean) Allows the user to use the same name for a file when editing the
    "!                         file name. 'Same name' refers to an already existing file name in the list.
    "!                         Default: false.
    "! @parameter show_separators              | (sap.m.ListSeparators) Defines whether separators are shown between list
    "!                         items. Default: All.
    "! @parameter upload_enabled               | (boolean) Enables the upload of a file. If property instantUpload is false
    "!                         it is not allowed to change uploadEnabled at runtime. Default: true.
    "! @parameter upload_url                   | (string) Specifies the URL where the uploaded files have to be stored.
    "!                         Default: ../../../upload.
    "! @parameter instant_upload               | (boolean) If false, no upload is triggered when a file is selected. In
    "!                         addition, if a file was selected, a new FileUploader instance is created to
    "!                         ensure that multiple files can be chosen. Default: true.
    "! @parameter number_of_attachments_text   | (string) Sets the title text in the toolbar of the list of attachments. To
    "!                         show as well the number of attachments in brackets like the default text
    "!                         does. The number of attachments could be retrieved via "getItems().length".
    "!                         If a new title is set, the default is deactivated. The default value is set
    "!                         to language-dependent "Attachments (n)".
    "! @parameter mode                         | (sap.m.ListMode) Defines the selection mode of the control (e.g. None,
    "!                         SingleSelect, MultiSelect, SingleSelectLeft, SingleSelectMaster). Since the
    "!                         UploadCollection reacts like a list for attachments, the API is close to
    "!                         the ListBase Interface. sap.m.ListMode.Delete mode is not supported and
    "!                         will be automatically set to sap.m.ListMode.None. In addition, if instant
    "!                         upload is set to false the mode sap.m.ListMode.MultiSelect is not supported
    "!                         and will be automatically set to sap.m.ListMode.None. Default: None.
    "! @parameter upload_button_invisible      | (boolean) If true, the button used for uploading files is invisible.
    "!                         Default: false.
    "! @parameter termination_enabled          | (boolean) If true, the button that is used to terminate the instant file
    "!                         upload gets visible. The button normally appears when a file is being
    "!                         uploaded. Default: true.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter change                       | (event) The event is triggered when files are selected in the FileUploader
    "!                         dialog. Applications can set parameters and headerParameters which will be
    "!                         dispatched to the embedded FileUploader control. Restriction: parameters
    "!                         and headerParameters are not supported by Internet Explorer 9.
    "! @parameter file_deleted                 | (event) The event is triggered when an uploaded attachment is selected and
    "!                         the Delete button is pressed.
    "! @parameter filename_length_exceed       | (event) The event is triggered when the name of a chosen file is longer
    "!                         than the value specified with the maximumFilenameLength property (only if
    "!                         provided by the application).
    "! @parameter file_renamed                 | (event) The event is triggered when the file name is changed.
    "! @parameter file_size_exceed             | (event) The event is triggered when the file size of an uploaded file is
    "!                         exceeded (only if the maxFileSize property was provided by the
    "!                         application). This event is not supported by Internet Explorer 9.
    "! @parameter type_missmatch               | (event) The event is triggered when the file type or the MIME type don't
    "!                         match the permitted types (only if the fileType property or the mimeType
    "!                         property are provided by the application).
    "! @parameter upload_complete              | (event) The event is triggered as soon as the upload request is completed.
    "! @parameter upload_terminated            | (event) The event is triggered as soon as the upload request was terminated
    "!                         by the user.
    "! @parameter before_upload_starts         | (event) The event is triggered before the actual upload starts. An event is
    "!                         fired per file. All the necessary header parameters should be set here.
    "! @parameter selection_change             | (event) Fires when selection is changed via user interaction inside the
    "!                         control.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS upload_collection
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_type                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        maximum_filename_length      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        maximum_file_size            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        mime_type                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        multiple                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        no_data_text                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        no_data_description          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        same_filename_allowed        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        show_separators              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_enabled               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_url                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        instant_upload               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        number_of_attachments_text   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        mode                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_button_invisible      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        termination_enabled          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        change                       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_deleted                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        filename_length_exceed       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_renamed                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_size_exceed             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        type_missmatch               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_complete              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_terminated            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        before_upload_starts         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selection_change             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.UploadCollectionItem</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.UploadCollectionItem
    "! Defines a structure of the element of the 'items' aggregation.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter document_id                  | (string) Specifies a unique identifier of the file (created by the
    "!                         application).
    "! @parameter file_name                    | (string) Specifies the name of the uploaded file.
    "! @parameter mime_type                    | (string) Specifies the MIME type of the file.
    "! @parameter thumbnail_url                | (string) Specifies the URL where the thumbnail of the file is located. This
    "!                         can also be an SAPUI5 icon URL.
    "! @parameter url                          | (string) Specifies the URL where the file is located. If the application
    "!                         doesn't provide a value for this property, the icon and the file name of
    "!                         the UploadCollectionItem are not clickable.
    "! @parameter enable_edit                  | (boolean) Enables/Disables the Edit button. If the value is true, the Edit
    "!                         button is enabled and the edit function can be used. If the value is false,
    "!                         the edit function is not available. Default: true.
    "! @parameter enable_delete                | (boolean) Enables/Disables the Delete button. If the value is true, the
    "!                         Delete button is enabled and the delete function can be used. If the value
    "!                         is false, the delete function is not available. Default: true.
    "! @parameter visible_edit                 | (boolean) Show/Hide the Edit button. If the value is true, the Edit button
    "!                         is visible. If the value is false, the Edit button is not visible. Default:
    "!                         true.
    "! @parameter visible_delete               | (boolean) Show/Hide the Delete button. If the value is true, the Delete
    "!                         button is visible. If the value is false, the Delete button is not visible.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter aria_label_for_picture       | (string) Aria label for the icon (or for the image).
    "! @parameter selected                     | (boolean) Defines the selected state of the UploadCollectionItem. Default:
    "!                         false.
    "! @parameter press                        | (event) This event is triggered when the user presses the filename link. If
    "!                         this event is provided, it overwrites the default behavior of opening the
    "!                         file.
    "! @parameter delete_press                 | (event) When a deletePress event handler is attached to the item and the
    "!                         user presses the delete button, this event is triggered. If this event is
    "!                         triggered, it overwrites the default delete behavior of UploadCollection
    "!                         and the fileDeleted event of UploadCollection is not triggered.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS upload_collection_item
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        document_id                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_name                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        mime_type                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        thumbnail_url                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        url                          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enable_edit                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        enable_delete                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible_edit                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible_delete               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        aria_label_for_picture       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        selected                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        press                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        delete_press                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.UploadCollectionParameter</p>
