    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.upload.UploadItem</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.upload.UploadItem
    "! sap.m.upload.UploadItem represents one item to be uploaded using the
    "! UploadSetwithTable Note: This element should only be used within the
    "! UploadSetwithTable plugin.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter file_name                    | (string) Specifies the name of the uploaded file.
    "! @parameter media_type                   | (string) Specifies the MIME type of the file.
    "! @parameter url                          | (string) Specifies the URL where the file is located.
    "! @parameter upload_url                   | (string) URL where the uploaded files are stored. If empty, uploadUrl from
    "!                         the uploader is considered.
    "! @parameter upload_state                 | (sap.m.UploadState) State of the item relevant to its upload process.
    "! @parameter previewable                  | (boolean) Specifies whether the item can be previewed. Default: true.
    "! @parameter file_size                    | (float) Specifies file size of the item in bytes. Default: 0.
    "! @parameter is_trusted_source            | (boolean) This property is used in the FilePreviewDialog to determine if
    "!                         the file is from a trusted source before displaying. This property must be
    "!                         set to true if the file is from a trusted source. Default: false.
    "! @parameter is_directory                 | (boolean) Specifies whether the item is a file or a directory. Used mainly
    "!                         for plugin with the tree table structure. Default: false.
    "! @parameter upload_progress              | (event) The event is fired every time an XHR request reports progress while
    "!                         uploading.
    "! @parameter upload_terminated            | (event) This event is fired right after the upload is terminated.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS upload_item
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_name                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        media_type                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        url                          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_url                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_state                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        previewable                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_size                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        is_trusted_source            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        is_directory                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_progress              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_terminated            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.upload.UploadItemConfiguration</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.upload.UploadItemConfiguration
    "! sap.m.UploadItemConfiguration represents the configuration for the items in the
    "! UploadSetwithTable plugin. The configuration template represents the paths in
    "! the model to the file name, mediaType, url, uploadUrl, previewable, and file
    "! size properties in reference to the UploadItem. This is essential for the plugin
    "! in understanding the structure of the model data bound to continue with
    "! operations. Note: Configuration is mandatory for the plugin to offer the
    "! features such as file preview, download, rename etc. The element must be used
    "! only within the UploadSetwithTable plugin.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter file_name_path               | (string) Specifies the path in the model to the file name
    "! @parameter media_type_path              | (string) Specifies the path in the model to the file mediaType.
    "! @parameter url_path                     | (string) Specifies the path in the model to the file URL. It is used to
    "!                         download/access the file.
    "! @parameter upload_url_path              | (string) Specifies the path in the model for upload URL. Used to upload the
    "!                         file.
    "! @parameter previewable_path             | (string) Specifies the path in the model to determine if the file uploaded
    "!                         can be previewed.
    "! @parameter file_size_path               | (string) Specifies path in the model to the file size.
    "! @parameter is_trusted_source_path       | (string) Specifies the path in the model to confirm if the file is from a
    "!                         trusted source. This is used to determine if the file is uploaded from a
    "!                         trusted source. If the file is uploaded from a trusted source, the file can
    "!                         be previewed. Set this property to the path in the model that determines if
    "!                         the file is uploaded from a trusted source.
    "! @parameter is_directory_path            | (string) Specifies the path in the model to confirm if it is a file or a
    "!                         directory. This is used to determine if the context is file or a directory.
    "!                         If it is a directory, it cannot be previewed. Set this property to the path
    "!                         in the model to determine if it is a file or a directory. The value of this
    "!                         path evaluated should be boolean.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS upload_item_configuration
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_name_path               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        media_type_path              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        url_path                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_url_path              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        previewable_path             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_size_path               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        is_trusted_source_path       TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        is_directory_path            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.upload.UploadSet</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.upload.UploadSet
    "! This control allows you to upload one or more files from your devices (desktop,
    "! tablet, or phone) and attach them to your application. This control builds on
    "! the sap.m.UploadCollection control, providing better handling of headers and
    "! requests, unified behavior of instant and deferred uploads, as well as improved
    "! progress indication. We now ensure that the control handles item insertion and
    "! deletion if the items aggregation is not bound to a model. It allows the
    "! connected model to not only manage the insertion and deletion updates but it
    "! also helps to avoid template-related issues and ensures better data handling.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter file_types                   | (string[]) Allowed file types for files to be uploaded. If this property is
    "!                         not set, any file can be uploaded.
    "! @parameter max_file_name_length         | (int) Maximum length of names of files to be uploaded. If set to null or 0
    "!                         , any files can be uploaded, regardless of their names length.
    "! @parameter max_file_size                | (float) Size limit in megabytes for files to be uploaded. If set to null or
    "!                         0 , files of any size can be uploaded.
    "! @parameter media_types                  | (string[]) Allowed media types for files to be uploaded. If this property
    "!                         is not set, any file can be uploaded.
    "! @parameter drag_drop_text               | (string) Defines custom text for the drag and drop text label.
    "! @parameter drag_drop_description        | (string) Defines custom text for the drag and drop description label.
    "! @parameter instant_upload               | (boolean) Defines whether the upload process should be triggered as soon as
    "!                         the file is added. If set to false , no upload is triggered when a file is
    "!                         added. Default: true.
    "! @parameter show_icons                   | (boolean) Defines whether file icons should be displayed. Default: true.
    "! @parameter termination_enabled          | (boolean) Defines whether it is allowed to terminate the upload process.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter upload_enabled               | (boolean) Defines whether the upload action is allowed. Default: true.
    "! @parameter upload_url                   | (string) URL where the uploaded files will be stored.
    "! @parameter upload_button_invisible      | (boolean) If set to true, the button used for uploading files become
    "!                         invisible. Default: false.
    "! @parameter same_filename_allowed        | (boolean) Allows the user to use the same name for a file while editing the
    "!                         file name. 'Same name' refers to an already existing file name in the list.
    "!                         Default: false.
    "! @parameter http_request_method          | (sap.m.upload.UploaderHttpRequestMethod) HTTP request method chosen for
    "!                         file upload. Default: Post.
    "! @parameter multiple                     | (boolean) Lets the user select multiple files from the same folder and then
    "!                         upload them. If multiple property is set to false, the control shows an
    "!                         error message if more than one file is chosen for drag & drop. Default:
    "!                         false.
    "! @parameter mode                         | (sap.m.ListMode) Defines the selection mode of the control (e.g. None,
    "!                         SingleSelect, MultiSelect, SingleSelectLeft, SingleSelectMaster). Since the
    "!                         UploadSet reacts like a list for attachments, the API is close to the
    "!                         ListBase Interface. sap.m.ListMode.Delete mode is not supported and will be
    "!                         automatically set to sap.m.ListMode.None. In addition, if instant upload is
    "!                         set to false the mode sap.m.ListMode.MultiSelect is not supported and will
    "!                         be automatically set to sap.m.ListMode.None. Default: MultiSelect.
    "! @parameter cloud_file_picker_enabled    | (boolean) Enables CloudFile picker feature to upload files from cloud.
    "!                         Default: false.
    "! @parameter cloud_file_picker_service_url | (sap.ui.core.URI) Url of the FileShare OData V4 service supplied for
    "!                         CloudFile picker control.
    "! @parameter cloud_file_picker_button_text | (string) The text of the CloudFile picker button. The default text is
    "!                         "Upload from cloud" (translated to the respective language).
    "! @parameter directory                    | (boolean) Lets the user upload entire files from directories and sub
    "!                         directories. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter after_item_added             | (event) This event is fired when a new file is added to the set of items to
    "!                         be uploaded.
    "! @parameter file_renamed                 | (event) The event is triggered when the file name is changed.
    "! @parameter after_item_removed           | (event) This event is fired after the item is removed on click of ok button
    "!                         in confirmation dialog.
    "! @parameter after_item_edited            | (event) This event is fired after item edit is confirmed.
    "! @parameter before_item_added            | (event) This event is fired just before a new file is added to the set of
    "!                         items to be uploaded.
    "! @parameter before_item_removed          | (event) This event is fired just before the confirmation dialog for
    "!                         'Remove' action is displayed.
    "! @parameter before_item_edited           | (event) This event is fired when the edit button is clicked for an item and
    "!                         no other item is being edited at the same time. If there is another item
    "!                         that has unsaved changes, the editing of the clicked item cannot be
    "!                         started.
    "! @parameter before_upload_starts         | (event) This event is fired right before the upload process begins.
    "! @parameter upload_completed             | (event) This event is fired right after the upload process is finished.
    "! @parameter before_upload_termination    | (event) This event is fired right before the upload is terminated.
    "! @parameter upload_terminated            | (event) This event is fired right after the upload is terminated.
    "! @parameter file_type_mismatch           | (event) This event is fired in either of the following cases: When a file
    "!                         that is selected to be uploaded fails to meet the file type restriction (
    "!                         fileType property). When the file type restriction changes, and the file to
    "!                         be uploaded fails to meet the new restriction.
    "! @parameter file_name_length_exceeded    | (event) This event is fired in either of the following cases: When a file
    "!                         that is selected to be uploaded fails to meet the file name length
    "!                         restriction specified in the maxFileNameLength property. When the file name
    "!                         length restriction changes, and the file to be uploaded fails to meet the
    "!                         new restriction. Listeners can use the item parameter to remove the
    "!                         incomplete item that failed to meet the restriction
    "! @parameter file_size_exceeded           | (event) This event is fired in either of the following cases: When a file
    "!                         that is selected to be uploaded fails to meet the file size restriction
    "!                         specified in the maxFileSize property. When the file size restriction
    "!                         changes, and the file to be uploaded fails to meet the new restriction.
    "!                         Listeners can use the item parameter to remove the incomplete item that
    "!                         failed to meet the restriction
    "! @parameter media_type_mismatch          | (event) This event is fired in either of the following cases: When a file
    "!                         that is selected to be uploaded fails to meet the media type restriction
    "!                         specified in the mediaTypes property. When the media type restriction
    "!                         changes, and the file to be uploaded fails to meet the new restriction.
    "! @parameter selection_changed            | (event) This event is fired simultaneously with the respective event in the
    "!                         inner sap.m.List control.
    "! @parameter item_drag_start              | (event) This event is fired when the user starts dragging an uploaded item.
    "! @parameter item_drop                    | (event) This event is fired when an uploaded item is dropped on the new
    "!                         list position.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS upload_set
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
