    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.upload.UploadSetToolbarPlaceholder</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.upload.UploadSetToolbarPlaceholder
    "! Used to create a customizable toolbar for the UploadSet. A FileUploader instance
    "! is required in the toolbar and it is placed by the application.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter busy                         | (boolean) Whether the control is currently in busy state. Default: false.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_delay         | (int) The delay in milliseconds, after which the busy indicator will show
    "!                         up for this control. Default: 1000.
    "! @parameter busy_indicator_size          | (sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize) The size of the BusyIndicator. For controls
    "!                         with a width smaller 3rem a sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Small should be
    "!                         used. If the size could vary in width and the width could get smaller than
    "!                         3rem, the sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Auto option could be used. The
    "!                         default is set to sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Medium For a full screen
    "!                         BusyIndicator use sap.ui.core.BusyIndicatorSize.Large . Default: Medium.
    "! @parameter visible                      | (boolean) Whether the control should be visible on the screen. If set to
    "!                         false, a placeholder will be rendered to mark the location of the invisible
    "!                         control in the DOM of the current page. The placeholder will be hidden and
    "!                         have zero dimensions ( display: none ). Also see InvisibleRenderer.
    "!                         Default: true.
    "! @parameter field_group_ids              | (string[]) The IDs of a logical field group that this control belongs to.
    "!                         All fields in a logical field group should share the same fieldGroupId .
    "!                         Once a logical field group is left, the validateFieldGroup event is fired.
    "!                         For backward compatibility with older releases, field group IDs are
    "!                         syntactically not limited, but it is suggested to use only valid
    "!                         sap.ui.core.IDs. See attachValidateFieldGroup or consult the Field Group
    "!                         documentation. Default: .
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS upload_set_toolbar_placeholder
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy                         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_delay         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        busy_indicator_size          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        visible                      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        field_group_ids              TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.plugins.UploadSetwithTable</p>
    "! https://ui5.sap.com/#/api/sap.m.plugins.UploadSetwithTable
    "! The UploadSetwithTable plugin enables uploading within a table when it is added
    "! as a dependent to the table control. This plugin provides an Upload button to
    "! upload files from the local file system. To do so, the user of the plugin must
    "! place Actions Placeholder control at the desired table area and then associate
    "! the actions of the plugin with the placeholder. The plugin provides the ability
    "! to upload files from the local system as well as from cloud file picker and
    "! includes other notable features such as validation, file preview, download. The
    "! following controls support this plugin: MDC Table Responsive Table Grid Table
    "! Tree Table Consider the following before using the plugin: It gets activated
    "! when it is added as a dependent to the table control. It gets deactivated when
    "! it is removed from the table control or when the table control is destroyed. It
    "! fires onActivated and onDeactivated events when it is activated and deactivated,
    "! respectively. Configuring the rowConfiguration aggregation (type
    "! UploadItemConfiguration) of this plugin is mandatory to use the features such as
    "! file preview, download etc. For the plugin to work with the tree table control,
    "! the isDirectoryPath property of the rowConfiguration aggregation must be set.
    "! This indicates if the context of the row is a directory or a file. It helps the
    "! plugin with the file preview feature. It works only with the table control when
    "! the table is bound to the model to perform the operations such as rename,
    "! download etc.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter file_types                   | (string[]) File types that are allowed to be uploaded. If this property is
    "!                         not set, any file can be uploaded.
    "! @parameter max_file_name_length         | (int) Defined maximum length for a name of files that are to be uploaded.
    "!                         If set to null or 0 , any file can be uploaded regardless length of its
    "!                         name.
    "! @parameter max_file_size                | (float) Defined size limit in megabytes for files that are to be uploaded.
    "!                         If set to null or 0 , files of any size can be uploaded.
    "! @parameter media_types                  | (string[]) Media types of files that are allowed to be uploaded. If this
    "!                         property is not set, any file can be uploaded.
    "! @parameter upload_url                   | (string) Url where the uploaded files are stored.
    "! @parameter http_request_method          | (sap.m.upload.UploaderHttpRequestMethod) HTTP request method chosen for
    "!                         file upload. Default: Post.
    "! @parameter multiple                     | (boolean) Lets the user select multiple files from the same folder and then
    "!                         upload them. If multiple property is set to false, the plugin shows an
    "!                         error message if more than one file is chosen for drag & drop. Default:
    "!                         false.
    "! @parameter upload_button_invisible      | (boolean) If set to true, the button used for uploading files becomes
    "!                         invisible. Default: false.
    "! @parameter upload_enabled               | (boolean) Defines whether the upload action is allowed. Default: true.
    "! @parameter item_validation_handler      | (function) Defines a callback function that is invoked when each UploadItem
    "!                         is queued up for upload. This callback is invoked with parameters and the
    "!                         callback is expected to return a promise to the plugin. Once the promise is
    "!                         resolved, the plugin initiates the upload process. Configure this property
    "!                         only when any additional configuration or validations are to be performed
    "!                         before the upload of each item. The upload process is triggered manually by
    "!                         resolving the promise returned to the plugin.
    "! @parameter directory                    | (boolean) Lets the user upload entire files from directories and sub
    "!                         directories. Default: false.
    "! @parameter cloud_file_picker_enabled    | (boolean) Enables CloudFile picker feature to upload files from cloud.
    "!                         Default: false.
    "! @parameter cloud_file_picker_service_url | (sap.ui.core.URI) Url of the FileShare OData V4 service supplied for
    "!                         CloudFile picker control.
    "! @parameter cloud_file_picker_button_text | (string) The text of the CloudFile picker button. The default text is
    "!                         "Upload from cloud" (translated to the respective language).
    "! @parameter file_name_validation_config  | (sap.m.plugins.UploadSetwithTable.FilenameValidationConfig) File name
    "!                         validation configuration. Set this property to configure the file name
    "!                         validation characters and the validation mode. This configuration is used
    "!                         to validate the file name when a file is selected for renaming. For the
    "!                         plugin to pick up this configuration, mode and characters of the property
    "!                         must be set to validate the file name. see mode to configure the file name
    "!                         validation mode. The default restricted filename character set is:
    "!                         \:/*?"<>|[] $
    "! @parameter item_renamed                 | (event) The event is triggered when the file name is changed.
    "! @parameter item_rename_canceled         | (event) The event is triggered when the file renaming process is canceled.
    "! @parameter before_upload_starts         | (event) This event is fired right before the upload process begins.
    "! @parameter upload_completed             | (event) This event is fired right after the upload process is finished.
    "!                         Based on the backend response of the application, listeners can use the
    "!                         parameters to determine if the upload was successful or if it failed.
    "! @parameter file_type_mismatch           | (event) This event is fired in either of the following cases: When a file
    "!                         that is selected to be uploaded fails to meet the file type restriction (
    "!                         fileType property). When the file type restriction changes, and the file to
    "!                         be uploaded fails to meet the new restriction.
    "! @parameter file_name_length_exceeded    | (event) This event is fired in either of the following cases: When a file
    "!                         that is selected to be uploaded fails to meet the file name length
    "!                         restriction specified in the maxFileNameLength property. When the file name
    "!                         length restriction changes, and the file to be uploaded fails to meet the
    "!                         new restriction.
    "! @parameter file_size_exceeded           | (event) This event is fired in either of the following cases: When a file
    "!                         that is selected to be uploaded fails to meet the file size restriction
    "!                         specified in the maxFileSize property. When the file size restriction
    "!                         changes, and the file to be uploaded fails to meet the new restriction.
    "! @parameter media_type_mismatch          | (event) This event is fired in either of the following cases: When a file
    "!                         that is selected to be uploaded fails to meet the media type restriction
    "!                         specified in the mediaTypes property. When the media type restriction
    "!                         changes, and the file to be uploaded fails to meet the new restriction.
    "! @parameter before_initiating_item_upload | (event) This event is fired just before initiating the file upload process
    "!                         when a file is selected to be uploaded. Use this event to set additional
    "!                         info dynamically, specific for each item before upload process is
    "!                         initiated.
    "! @parameter on_activated                 | (event) This event is fired when plugin is activated.
    "! @parameter on_deactivated               | (event) This event is fired when plugin is deactivated.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS upload_setwith_table
      IMPORTING
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_types                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        max_file_name_length         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        max_file_size                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        media_types                  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_url                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        http_request_method          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        multiple                     TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_button_invisible      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_enabled               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        item_validation_handler      TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        directory                    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        cloud_file_picker_enabled    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        cloud_file_picker_service_url TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        cloud_file_picker_button_text TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_name_validation_config  TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        item_renamed                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        item_rename_canceled         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        before_upload_starts         TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_completed             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_type_mismatch           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_name_length_exceeded    TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        file_size_exceeded           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        media_type_mismatch          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        before_initiating_item_upload TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        on_activated                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        on_deactivated               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">Duplicate: uploader (2 variants) -> ns</p>
    "! - sap.m.upload.Uploader (ns='')
    "! - Aggregation <uploader> (ns='')
    "! Namespace prefixes: '' = sap.m, 'core' = sap.ui.core, 'mvc' = sap.ui.core.mvc, 'l' = sap.ui.layout, 'form' = sap.ui.layout.form, 'table' = sap.ui.table
    "! @parameter ns                           | (string) Namespace prefix. Allowed '', 'core', 'mvc', 'l', 'form', 'table'
    "!                         ('' is sap.m default). Variants: sap.m.upload.Uploader ('') |
    "!                         aggregation:uploader (''). Pass prefix directly.
    "! @parameter id                           | (string) Unique control identifier
    "! @parameter class                        | (string) CSS class names
    "! @parameter upload_url                   | (string) URL where the next file is going to be uploaded to.
    "! @parameter download_url                 | (string) URL where the next file is going to be download from.
    "! @parameter http_request_method          | (sap.m.upload.UploaderHttpRequestMethod) HTTP request method chosen for
    "!                         file upload. Default: Post.
    "! @parameter use_multipart                | (boolean) This property decides the type of request. If set to "true", the
    "!                         request gets sent as a multipart/form-data request instead of file only
    "!                         request. Default: false.
    "! @parameter upload_started               | (event) The event is fired just after the POST request was sent.
    "! @parameter upload_progressed            | (event) The event is fired every time an XHR request reports progress in
    "!                         uploading.
    "! @parameter upload_completed             | (event) The event is fired when an XHR request reports successful
    "!                         completion of upload process.
    "! @parameter upload_aborted               | (event) The event is fired when an XHR request reports its abortion.
    "! @parameter result                       | (REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder) Reference to builder
    METHODS uploader
      IMPORTING
        ns                           TYPE string OPTIONAL
        id                           TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        class                        TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_url                   TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        download_url                 TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        http_request_method          TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        use_multipart                TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_started               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_progressed            TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_completed             TYPE clike OPTIONAL
        upload_aborted               TYPE clike OPTIONAL
      RETURNING
        VALUE(result) TYPE REF TO z2fiori_cl_xml_view_builder.

    "! <p class="shorttext synchronized" lang="en">sap.m.upload.UploaderTableItem</p>
